<graph edgedefault="undirected"><node id="Unified Knowledge Graph">
  <data key="d0">Unified Knowledge Graph</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">A comprehensive knowledge graph denoted as G = (ν, E) that captures both multimodal contextual relationships and text-based semantic connections after graph fusion.&lt;SEP&gt;The Unified Knowledge Graph, denoted as G, is a structural knowledge representation that encodes explicit relationships and multi-hop reasoning patterns across heterogeneous modalities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ea106f7be2831088c0a1118ecb40eee8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eac0008c777dab7291aec281277e77a1</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514159</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Embedding Table">
  <data key="d0">Embedding Table</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">A comprehensive table that encompasses all components generated during the indexing process, mapping entities, relations, and chunks to dense representations.&lt;SEP&gt;The Embedding Table, denoted as τ, stores dense vector representations of knowledge components and enables semantic similarity search.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ea106f7be2831088c0a1118ecb40eee8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eac0008c777dab7291aec281277e77a1</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514159</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Retrieval Index">
  <data key="d0">Retrieval Index</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The complete retrieval index consisting of the unified knowledge graph and the embedding table, providing structural knowledge representation and dense vector space for cross-modal similarity search.&lt;SEP&gt;The Retrieval Index, denoted as T = (G, T), combines the unified knowledge graph and embedding table to provide both structural knowledge representation and dense vector space for cross-modal similarity search.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ea106f7be2831088c0a1118ecb40eee8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eac0008c777dab7291aec281277e77a1</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514159</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cross-Modal Hybrid Retrieval">
  <data key="d0">Cross-Modal Hybrid Retrieval</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Cross-Modal Hybrid Retrieval is a mechanism that combines structural knowledge navigation with semantic similarity matching to enable effective retrieval across heterogeneous modalities. It leverages both a unified knowledge graph and an embedding table to perform efficient cross-modal similarity search, allowing textual queries to access non-textual content through shared embeddings. By integrating graph-based retrieval with cross-modal integration, the approach identifies relevant knowledge components for a given user query and supports reasoning over heterogeneous content.

This mechanism is employed by RAG-Anything, where it contributes to the system's effectiveness in long-document reasoning tasks. Within the RAG-Anything pipeline, cross-modal hybrid retrieval operates as a retrieval stage that follows the graph fusion step. Its contribution has been validated by ablation study results.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ea106f7be2831088c0a1118ecb40eee8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de93d4b6f02e5ae737b9b9e8142401cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a43d425aea6f4b6c0edc38f28595f400&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dded67fd8182de2201aa35ccbb4c8cd9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eac0008c777dab7291aec281277e77a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-885744df4898cd552f1960ba1b518cb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-162b82c942fb3baf527c7b1adf1ed920&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21f9c375189978b339552ff8ff4ba819</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514430</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Modality-Aware Query Encoding">
  <data key="d0">Modality-Aware Query Encoding</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Modality-Aware Query Encoding performs query analysis to extract lexical cues and potential modality preferences, then computes a unified text embedding using the same encoder employed during indexing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ea106f7be2831088c0a1118ecb40eee8</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514159</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Structural Knowledge Navigation">
  <data key="d0">Structural Knowledge Navigation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Structural knowledge navigation is a component of the cross-modal hybrid retrieval mechanism that leverages explicit graph relationships to capture multi-hop reasoning patterns.&lt;SEP&gt;Structural Knowledge Navigation exploits structural properties encoded within the unified knowledge graph, employing keyword matching and entity recognition followed by strategic neighborhood expansion to capture explicit relationships and multi-hop reasoning patterns.&lt;SEP&gt;Structural Knowledge Navigation is a retrieval mechanism that interacts with the Knowledge Graph.&lt;SEP&gt;A retrieval capability supported by the union over V, E, and c_j, allowing navigation of structural knowledge elements.&lt;SEP&gt;Structural knowledge navigation is a component of the cross-modal hybrid retrieval architecture that enables leveraging explicit relationships across modalities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ea106f7be2831088c0a1118ecb40eee8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dded67fd8182de2201aa35ccbb4c8cd9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-885744df4898cd552f1960ba1b518cb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cb795e1c89d1938a0fcb44cbec5be74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-808bf767f815e787e09b6b3e8a122b71</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514429</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Semantic Similarity Matching">
  <data key="d0">Semantic Similarity Matching</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Semantic similarity matching is a component of the cross-modal hybrid retrieval mechanism that employs dense vector representations to identify semantically relevant content.&lt;SEP&gt;Semantic Similarity Matching conducts dense vector similarity search between the query embedding and all components stored in the embedding table, enabling fine-grained semantic matching across all modalities.&lt;SEP&gt;Semantic Similarity Matching is a retrieval mechanism that interacts with the Vector Database.&lt;SEP&gt;A retrieval capability supported by the union over V, E, and c_j, allowing matching of knowledge components by semantic similarity.&lt;SEP&gt;Semantic similarity matching is a component of the cross-modal hybrid retrieval architecture that enables leveraging implicit semantic connections across modalities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ea106f7be2831088c0a1118ecb40eee8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dded67fd8182de2201aa35ccbb4c8cd9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-885744df4898cd552f1960ba1b518cb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cb795e1c89d1938a0fcb44cbec5be74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-808bf767f815e787e09b6b3e8a122b71</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514429</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Candidate Pool Unification">
  <data key="d0">Candidate Pool Unification</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Candidate Pool Unification combines retrieval candidates from both structural and semantic pathways into a comprehensive candidate pool for principled ranking.&lt;SEP&gt;Candidate pool unification is the process of merging retrieval results into a single pool for subsequent fusion and ranking.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ea106f7be2831088c0a1118ecb40eee8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e906fa59bd4a41ccc46a928ffee1aa2</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514436</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Multi-Signal Fusion Scoring">
  <data key="d0">Multi-Signal Fusion Scoring</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Multi-Signal Fusion Scoring integrates structural importance from graph topology, semantic similarity scores from embedding space, and query-inferred modality preferences to produce final ranked candidates.&lt;SEP&gt;Multi-signal fusion scoring is the technique used to fuse and rank the unified candidate pool to produce the top-ranked retrieval candidates C*(q).</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ea106f7be2831088c0a1118ecb40eee8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e906fa59bd4a41ccc46a928ffee1aa2</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514436</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hybrid Retrieval Integration">
  <data key="d0">Hybrid Retrieval Integration</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Hybrid Retrieval Integration leverages the complementary strengths of both knowledge graphs and dense representations to provide comprehensive coverage of relevant multimodal knowledge.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ea106f7be2831088c0a1118ecb40eee8</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514160</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Synthesis Stage">
  <data key="d0">Synthesis Stage</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The Synthesis Stage systematically combines retrieved multimodal knowledge into comprehensive, evidence-grounded responses by building structured textual context from top-ranked retrieval candidates.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ea106f7be2831088c0a1118ecb40eee8</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514160</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Building Textual Context">
  <data key="d0">Building Textual Context</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Building Textual Context concatenates textual representations of all retrieved components, including entity summaries, relationship descriptions, and chunk contents, with appropriate delimiters to indicate modality types and hierarchical origins.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ea106f7be2831088c0a1118ecb40eee8</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514160</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Multimodal Question Answering">
  <data key="d0">Multimodal Question Answering</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Multimodal Question Answering requires preserving rich visual semantics while maintaining coherent grounding across heterogeneous knowledge sources.&lt;SEP&gt;Multimodal question answering is the core idea embodied by the equation, preserving rich visual semantics while maintaining coherent grounding across heterogeneous knowledge sources.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ea106f7be2831088c0a1118ecb40eee8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e906fa59bd4a41ccc46a928ffee1aa2</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514436</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="RAG">
  <data key="d0">RAG</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Traditional RAG methods rely on semantic similarity within single modalities and face significant limitations when dealing with multimodal documents.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ea106f7be2831088c0a1118ecb40eee8</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514160</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="User Query">
  <data key="d0">User Query</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">A user query, denoted as q, is the input for which relevant knowledge components are identified during the retrieval stage.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ea106f7be2831088c0a1118ecb40eee8</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514160</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Query Embedding">
  <data key="d0">Query Embedding</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The Query Embedding, denoted as e_q, is a unified text embedding computed from the user query using the same encoder employed during indexing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ea106f7be2831088c0a1118ecb40eee8</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514160</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Structural Candidate Set">
  <data key="d0">Structural Candidate Set</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The Structural Candidate Set, denoted as C_str(q), contains relevant entities, relationships, and associated content chunks obtained through structural knowledge navigation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ea106f7be2831088c0a1118ecb40eee8</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514160</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Semantic Candidate Set">
  <data key="d0">Semantic Candidate Set</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The Semantic Candidate Set, denoted as C_seman(q), contains the top-k most semantically similar chunks ranked by cosine similarity scores from semantic similarity matching.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ea106f7be2831088c0a1118ecb40eee8</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514160</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Unified Candidate Pool">
  <data key="d0">Unified Candidate Pool</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The Unified Candidate Pool, denoted as C(q), is the union of structural and semantic candidate sets, providing comprehensive coverage of both structurally and semantically relevant knowledge.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ea106f7be2831088c0a1118ecb40eee8</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514160</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Final Ranked Candidates">
  <data key="d0">Final Ranked Candidates</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The Final Ranked Candidates, denoted as C*(q), are the output of multi-signal fusion scoring that balance structural knowledge relationships with semantic relevance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ea106f7be2831088c0a1118ecb40eee8</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514160</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Embedding Function">
  <data key="d0">Embedding Function</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The Embedding Function, denoted as (·), is tailored for each component type to generate embeddings for knowledge components.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ea106f7be2831088c0a1118ecb40eee8</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514160</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Multimodal Documents">
  <data key="d0">Multimodal Documents</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Multimodal Documents contain visual, mathematical, tabular, and textual elements with rich interconnections that traditional RAG methods fail to capture.&lt;SEP&gt;Documents containing text, figures, tables, and equations, from which atomic content chunks c_j are extracted.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ea106f7be2831088c0a1118ecb40eee8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-885744df4898cd552f1960ba1b518cb4</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514429</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Modality Preferences">
  <data key="d0">Modality Preferences</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Modality Preferences are potential preferences for specific modalities embedded within a user query, inferred through lexical cues such as terms like "figure," "chart," "table," or "equation."</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ea106f7be2831088c0a1118ecb40eee8</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514161</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Encoder">
  <data key="d0">Encoder</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The Encoder is employed during indexing and reused for computing the query embedding to ensure consistency between query and knowledge representations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ea106f7be2831088c0a1118ecb40eee8</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514161</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cosine Similarity">
  <data key="d0">Cosine Similarity</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Cosine Similarity is used to rank the top-k most semantically similar chunks in the semantic similarity matching pathway.&lt;SEP&gt;A similarity measure used to compare queries and knowledge components within the unified vector space provided by the embedding table.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ea106f7be2831088c0a1118ecb40eee8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-885744df4898cd552f1960ba1b518cb4</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514429</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Language Model">
  <data key="d0">Language Model</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The Language Model parses and reasons over heterogeneous knowledge from the structured textual context constructed during the synthesis stage.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ea106f7be2831088c0a1118ecb40eee8</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514161</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Structural Importance">
  <data key="d0">Structural Importance</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Structural Importance is a relevance signal derived from graph topology used in multi-signal fusion scoring.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ea106f7be2831088c0a1118ecb40eee8</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514161</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Semantic Similarity Scores">
  <data key="d0">Semantic Similarity Scores</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Semantic Similarity Scores are relevance signals from embedding space used in multi-signal fusion scoring.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ea106f7be2831088c0a1118ecb40eee8</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514161</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lexical Analysis">
  <data key="d0">Lexical Analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Lexical Analysis is used to obtain query-inferred modality preferences during multi-signal fusion scoring.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ea106f7be2831088c0a1118ecb40eee8</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514161</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Entity Summaries">
  <data key="d0">Entity Summaries</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Entity Summaries are textual representations of retrieved entities concatenated during the building of textual context.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ea106f7be2831088c0a1118ecb40eee8</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514161</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Relationship Descriptions">
  <data key="d0">Relationship Descriptions</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Relationship Descriptions are textual representations of retrieved relationships concatenated during the building of textual context.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ea106f7be2831088c0a1118ecb40eee8</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514161</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Chunk Contents">
  <data key="d0">Chunk Contents</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Chunk Contents are textual representations of retrieved content chunks concatenated during the building of textual context.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ea106f7be2831088c0a1118ecb40eee8</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514161</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="RAG-Anything">
  <data key="d0">RAG-Anything</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">RAG-Anything is a unified, all-in-one retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) framework designed to reimagine multimodal knowledge representation and retrieval. It treats text, images, tables, and equations as first-class entities, reconceptualizing multimodal content as interconnected knowledge entities. The framework extends GraphRAG to all modalities and unifies heterogeneous multimodal knowledge by decomposing content into atomic content units.

At its core, RAG-Anything employs a dual-graph construction strategy, building both cross-modal and text-based knowledge graphs that are merged via entity alignment. This produces modality-aware graphs that preserve essential relationships within multimodal documents, enabling precise reasoning over complex layouts. Complementing this is a cross-modal hybrid retrieval mechanism, which together with the dual-graph approach forms the framework's central architecture for cross-modal retrieval and reasoning. The framework also includes a dense representation generation step in its indexing pipeline and constructs a cross-modal knowledge graph (as described by Equation 4). Additional features include context-aware multimodal prompting.

RAG-Anything demonstrates superior performance on long documents and complex multimodal layouts, particularly where relevant evidence is dispersed across multiple modalities and sections. It has been evaluated using the DocBench and MMLongBench benchmarks, including an ablation study on DocBench. On MMLongBench, it achieves the best results in information-dense domains such as Research Reports and Financial Reports, with consistent improvements across all document length categories: accuracy gains of 3.4 points for 11–50 pages, 9.3 points for 51–100 pages, and 7.9 points for 101–200 pages. It outperforms MM-GraphRAG on long-document reasoning tasks.

The framework excels at complex visual reasoning and tabular navigation by constructing structured graph representations of visual elements (such as bar plots) and tabular data, enabling precise alignment between visual and textual information. However, in documented failure cases, RAG-Anything produced an incorrect answer regarding the NER label generation sequence and failed to correctly interpret an irregular table in a cross-modal noise scenario. The framework's documentation also addresses challenges and future directions for multimodal RAG.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-de93d4b6f02e5ae737b9b9e8142401cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7aefd567d430c404aab77872282400eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d4727f37ea1b30518f13dc89ffc7ea1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a43d425aea6f4b6c0edc38f28595f400&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dded67fd8182de2201aa35ccbb4c8cd9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5f0a5a74b5a4eac43772c74649ca651&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eac0008c777dab7291aec281277e77a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7eea2cc84733111d4a7fedb10d7083b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-885744df4898cd552f1960ba1b518cb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-840e794a234c66ff0680c138d02d19ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cb795e1c89d1938a0fcb44cbec5be74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-306f65a0f4295fa49788ecf8659d4b81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0238e7dae37f77eecdb2fe491a026dc0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4b25ee421d57dc99861b0d26ac02b54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d556fb722f8eac5fc92376e70d34e60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17a576920c675eca791231767d46477b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5eb0987c79c221cedef1a930b87f821f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37ff528cd8f38cd79fa57c96fab4a7c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-808bf767f815e787e09b6b3e8a122b71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a908e853be8da852064e031c68c78242&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1f82685779db44d104d20c4e16fe8b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-162b82c942fb3baf527c7b1adf1ed920&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89ff37f1683bc8edc5276effd3646dee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-960c77c28320f020a2006dba07f70f59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-301da515d50a3a0d178c0683bee24465&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3ef854a849174a61602e3f9d4a8eac1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21f9c375189978b339552ff8ff4ba819</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514429</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MM-GraphRAG">
  <data key="d0">MM-GraphRAG</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">MM-GraphRAG is a baseline method that exhibits comparable performance to RAG-Anything on shorter documents but falls behind as document length grows, and only considers image modality entities.&lt;SEP&gt;MM-GraphRAG is a baseline framework that exhibits comparable performance to RAG-Anything on shorter documents but falls behind as document length grows.&lt;SEP&gt;MM-GraphRAG is a RAG method that exhibits comparable performance to RAG-Anything on shorter documents but falls behind as document length increases.&lt;SEP&gt;MM-GraphRAG is a RAG method that shows comparable performance to RAG-Anything on shorter documents but falls behind as document length increases.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-de93d4b6f02e5ae737b9b9e8142401cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cb795e1c89d1938a0fcb44cbec5be74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-162b82c942fb3baf527c7b1adf1ed920&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-301da515d50a3a0d178c0683bee24465</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514430</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="DocBench">
  <data key="d0">DocBench</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">DocBench is a challenging multimodal Document Question Answering benchmark designed to evaluate model performance across varying document lengths and to validate the effectiveness of the RAG-Anything approach. It comprises 229 documents spanning five domains and document types, with an average length of 66 pages and approximately 46,377 tokens per document. The benchmark includes 1,102 expert-crafted question-answer pairs. Its documents encompass medium- to long-length materials across various domains, including legal, governmental, and financial files, with financial reports averaging 192 pages and news consisting of concise single-page newspapers; detailed statistics are provided in Table 5.

DocBench serves as an evaluation dataset for the RAG-Anything framework and its variants, enabling sophisticated visual interpretation and evidence-grounded response generation. On this benchmark, RAG-Anything outperforms MM-GraphRAG by over 13 points on documents exceeding 100 pages, a performance gap that expands dramatically at that document length. Representative cases from DocBench have been analyzed to demonstrate how RAG-Anything leverages structural information and intra-modal structures.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-de93d4b6f02e5ae737b9b9e8142401cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d4727f37ea1b30518f13dc89ffc7ea1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dded67fd8182de2201aa35ccbb4c8cd9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cb795e1c89d1938a0fcb44cbec5be74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-306f65a0f4295fa49788ecf8659d4b81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e906fa59bd4a41ccc46a928ffee1aa2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17a576920c675eca791231767d46477b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5eb0987c79c221cedef1a930b87f821f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1f82685779db44d104d20c4e16fe8b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cdd68412adb670ecbcf365fd5720250&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-162b82c942fb3baf527c7b1adf1ed920&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3ef854a849174a61602e3f9d4a8eac1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21f9c375189978b339552ff8ff4ba819</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514432</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MMLongBench">
  <data key="d0">MMLongBench</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">MMLongBench is a challenging long-context multimodal document comprehension benchmark designed to evaluate document question answering and retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) frameworks. It comprises 135 documents spanning 7 document types, with an average length of 47.5 pages and 21,214 tokens per document, accompanied by 1,082 expert-annotated questions. The benchmark's document composition covers a broad spectrum of types and lengths, including research reports, tutorials, academic papers, guidebooks, brochures, and administrative files, with detailed dataset statistics summarized in Table 6, where it is referenced alongside DocBench.

MMLongBench serves as an evaluation platform for assessing method performance across seven document domains and across documents of varying lengths, measuring overall accuracy and enabling sophisticated visual interpretation and evidence-grounded response generation. It is notably used to validate the effectiveness of the RAG-Anything approach, which demonstrates consistent accuracy improvements across all document length categories and achieves the best results in information-dense domains such as Research Reports and Financial Reports, outperforming baselines like MM-GraphRAG.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-de93d4b6f02e5ae737b9b9e8142401cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d4727f37ea1b30518f13dc89ffc7ea1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dded67fd8182de2201aa35ccbb4c8cd9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cb795e1c89d1938a0fcb44cbec5be74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-306f65a0f4295fa49788ecf8659d4b81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e906fa59bd4a41ccc46a928ffee1aa2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5eb0987c79c221cedef1a930b87f821f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-86f8b3b086da6cca91c5573b8ff551ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1f82685779db44d104d20c4e16fe8b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cdd68412adb670ecbcf365fd5720250&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-162b82c942fb3baf527c7b1adf1ed920&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-301da515d50a3a0d178c0683bee24465&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b8b33a1f15bc5b31bb493efd3ec933a</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514432</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dual-Graph Construction">
  <data key="d0">Dual-Graph Construction</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Dual-Graph Construction is a core architectural strategy and mechanism employed by RAG-Anything, designed to bridge cross-modal understanding with fine-grained textual semantics by building complementary knowledge graphs. It operates by constructing a cross-modal knowledge graph and a text-based knowledge graph, which are then merged through entity alignment to achieve a richer, unified knowledge representation. This approach captures both structural and cross-modal relationships within multimodal documents while preserving semantic alignment and structural context.

The technique is integrated within RAG-Anything's structured context injection mechanism, where it supports cross-page entity alignment. It is enabled as a subsequent process following the atomic units provided by document decomposition. Dual-Graph Construction contributes significantly to RAG-Anything's effectiveness in long-document reasoning tasks, and it is a component that is bypassed in the Chunk-Only variant of the system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-de93d4b6f02e5ae737b9b9e8142401cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a43d425aea6f4b6c0edc38f28595f400&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dded67fd8182de2201aa35ccbb4c8cd9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cb795e1c89d1938a0fcb44cbec5be74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0efdf5167592c14e899f82452298f2ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-808bf767f815e787e09b6b3e8a122b71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-162b82c942fb3baf527c7b1adf1ed920&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-301da515d50a3a0d178c0683bee24465&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21f9c375189978b339552ff8ff4ba819</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514433</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Chunk-Only">
  <data key="d0">Chunk-Only</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Chunk-only is an ablation variant that bypasses graph construction entirely and relies solely on traditional chunk-based retrieval, achieving only 60.0% accuracy.&lt;SEP&gt;Chunk-Only is a model variant that bypasses dual-graph construction and relies solely on traditional chunk-based retrieval, achieving the lowest overall accuracy of 60.0%.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-de93d4b6f02e5ae737b9b9e8142401cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21f9c375189978b339552ff8ff4ba819</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514450</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reranker">
  <data key="d0">Reranker</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The reranker is a cross-modal reranking component of RAG-Anything whose removal yields only a modest decline to 62.4% accuracy, indicating it provides marginal gains.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-de93d4b6f02e5ae737b9b9e8142401cd</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
