</node>
<node id="Ablation Studies">
  <data key="d0">Ablation Studies</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Ablation studies conducted on RAG-Anything reveal that graph-based knowledge representation provides the primary performance gains.&lt;SEP&gt;Ablation studies are systematic experiments conducted to isolate and quantify the contributions of key architectural components in RAG-Anything.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-de93d4b6f02e5ae737b9b9e8142401cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dded67fd8182de2201aa35ccbb4c8cd9</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514162</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="GraphRAG">
  <data key="d0">GraphRAG</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">An established text-centric extraction pipeline methodology referenced as a basis for constructing text-based knowledge graphs.&lt;SEP&gt;GraphRAG is an earlier method that introduced explicit relational modeling through graph structures to improve retrieval efficiency and reasoning accuracy.&lt;SEP&gt;GraphRAG is a graph-based retrieval-augmented generation approach that introduced explicit relational modeling to improve retrieval efficiency and reasoning accuracy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-de93d4b6f02e5ae737b9b9e8142401cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5f0a5a74b5a4eac43772c74649ca651&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eac0008c777dab7291aec281277e77a1</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514162</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Large Language Models">
  <data key="d0">Large Language Models</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Large Language Models (LLMs) are AI systems with exceptional reasoning capabilities whose knowledge remains static and bounded by training data cutoffs.&lt;SEP&gt;Large Language Models are static language models that RAG systems transform into adaptive, knowledge-aware systems by expanding their knowledge boundaries.&lt;SEP&gt;Large language models struggle with long-context inputs and multi-hop queries, failing to precisely locate dispersed evidence.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-de93d4b6f02e5ae737b9b9e8142401cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a43d425aea6f4b6c0edc38f28595f400&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dded67fd8182de2201aa35ccbb4c8cd9</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514162</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Graph-Enhanced Retrieval-Augmented Generation">
  <data key="d0">Graph-Enhanced Retrieval-Augmented Generation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Graph-enhanced retrieval-augmented generation is a research direction that addresses limitations of large language models by introducing explicit relational modeling through graph structures.&lt;SEP&gt;Graph-enhanced RAG uses graph structures to introduce explicit relational modeling, improving retrieval efficiency and reasoning accuracy for long-context and multi-hop queries.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-de93d4b6f02e5ae737b9b9e8142401cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5f0a5a74b5a4eac43772c74649ca651</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514162</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Multi-Panel Figure Interpretation">
  <data key="d0">Multi-Panel Figure Interpretation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Multi-panel figure interpretation is a case study demonstrating how RAG-Anything constructs a visual-layout graph to distinguish between related panels in complex visualizations.&lt;SEP&gt;Multi-panel figure interpretation is a case examining how researchers compare results across experimental conditions presented in multi-panel visualizations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-de93d4b6f02e5ae737b9b9e8142401cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17a576920c675eca791231767d46477b</data>
