</node>
<node id="GloVe + LSTM – Attention">
  <data key="d0">GloVe + LSTM – Attention</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">GloVe + LSTM – Attention is a model combination achieving the highest AUPRC value of 0.506 for the Evidence Inference dataset.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7aefd567d430c404aab77872282400eb</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514163</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Vision Analysis Prompt">
  <data key="d0">Vision Analysis Prompt</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Vision Analysis Prompt orchestrates comprehensive image-context integration by capturing compositional elements, object relationships, visual attributes, stylistic features, dynamic actions, and technical components while connecting to accompanying text.&lt;SEP&gt;The Vision Analysis Prompt is a structured prompt shown in a code editor that directs a model to systematically capture compositional elements, object relationships, visual attributes, stylistic features, dynamic actions, and technical components while connecting them to accompanying text.&lt;SEP&gt;The Vision Analysis Prompt is a prompt for context-aware image interpretation and knowledge extraction, referenced as Figure 7.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7aefd567d430c404aab77872282400eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7eea2cc84733111d4a7fedb10d7083b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-840e794a234c66ff0680c138d02d19ef</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514427</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Table Analysis Prompt">
  <data key="d0">Table Analysis Prompt</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Table Analysis Prompt structures systematic tabular content decomposition across structural organization, column semantics, critical values, statistical patterns, and contextual relevance.&lt;SEP&gt;The Table Analysis Prompt structures systematic tabular content decomposition across structural organization, column semantics, critical values, statistical patterns, and contextual relevance.&lt;SEP&gt;The Table Analysis Prompt is a text-based prompt template that instructs a model to analyze table content considering surrounding context and return a JSON response with detailed_description and entity_info fields, including placeholders for context, image path, caption, body, and footnotes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7aefd567d430c404aab77872282400eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7eea2cc84733111d4a7fedb10d7083b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-840e794a234c66ff0680c138d02d19ef</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514427</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Equation Analysis Prompt">
  <data key="d0">Equation Analysis Prompt</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Equation Analysis Prompt prioritizes semantic interpretation of mathematical expressions, analyzing variable definitions, operational logic, theoretical foundations, inter-formula relationships, and practical applications.&lt;SEP&gt;The Equation Analysis Prompt prioritizes semantic interpretation of mathematical expressions, analyzing variable definitions, operational logic, theoretical foundations, inter-formula relationships, and practical applications.&lt;SEP&gt;The Equation Analysis Prompt prioritizes semantic interpretation over syntactic restatement of mathematical expressions, covering variable definitions, operational logic, theoretical foundations, inter-formula relationships, and practical applications.&lt;SEP&gt;The Equation Analysis Prompt is a structured prompt template designed to instruct an AI model to analyze a mathematical equation and return a JSON response, prioritizing semantic interpretation over syntactic restatement of mathematical expressions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7aefd567d430c404aab77872282400eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7eea2cc84733111d4a7fedb10d7083b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-840e794a234c66ff0680c138d02d19ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d556fb722f8eac5fc92376e70d34e60</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514427</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="GPT-4o-mini">
  <data key="d0">GPT-4o-mini</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">GPT-4o-mini is a powerful multimodal language model with native text and image understanding capabilities and a 128K token context window. It serves as a backbone LLM and baseline in experimental frameworks, and is used to conduct all accuracy evaluations throughout these frameworks, ensuring consistent, reliable, and consistent assessment standards.

As a method, GPT-4o-mini was evaluated on the DocBench dataset, achieving an overall accuracy of 51.2%, and on MMLongBench, achieving an overall accuracy of 33.5%. As a baseline model, it demonstrated several incorrect responses across various tasks: it incorrectly identified VAE as having clearer separation in a multi-panel figure interpretation case; it incorrectly answered DKK 32,928 million for Novo Nordisk's wages and salaries in 2020; it provided an incorrect answer regarding the lowest accuracy GCAN configuration for Twitter15; and it incorrectly identified the BERT-to-BERT model with an AUPRC of 0.455 as the highest performer for the Evidence Inference dataset. Additionally, GPT-4o-mini was evaluated in a multimodal RAG failure case, producing an incorrect answer about the NER label generation sequence, and in a cross-modal noise case, providing an incorrect answer regarding joint goal accuracy improvements in the Train domain.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7aefd567d430c404aab77872282400eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d4727f37ea1b30518f13dc89ffc7ea1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49961962320a3499cad5000e71cf7f3e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7eea2cc84733111d4a7fedb10d7083b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-306f65a0f4295fa49788ecf8659d4b81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4b25ee421d57dc99861b0d26ac02b54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d556fb722f8eac5fc92376e70d34e60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17a576920c675eca791231767d46477b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37ff528cd8f38cd79fa57c96fab4a7c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a908e853be8da852064e031c68c78242&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89ff37f1683bc8edc5276effd3646dee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3ef854a849174a61602e3f9d4a8eac1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b8b33a1f15bc5b31bb493efd3ec933a</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514426</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Text-Centric Retrieval Bias">
  <data key="d0">Text-Centric Retrieval Bias</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Text-centric retrieval bias is a limitation where systems preferentially access textual sources even when queries explicitly require visual information.&lt;SEP&gt;Text-Centric Retrieval Bias is a failure pattern where systems exhibit strong preference for textual sources even when queries explicitly demand visual information, revealing inadequate cross-modal attention.&lt;SEP&gt;Text-centric retrieval bias is a systemic issue where RAG systems show pronounced bias toward textual passages, particularly when visual content lacks exact keyword matches, persisting even when queries explicitly prioritize visual sources.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7aefd567d430c404aab77872282400eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5f0a5a74b5a4eac43772c74649ca651&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37ff528cd8f38cd79fa57c96fab4a7c2</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514438</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Document Structure Processing Challenges">
  <data key="d0">Document Structure Processing Challenges</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Document Structure Processing Challenges is a failure pattern where systems struggle with complex layouts and nonlinear information flows, exposing limitations in spatial reasoning and contextual understanding.&lt;SEP&gt;Document structure processing challenges refer to systems struggling with complex layouts and nonlinear information flows, exposing limitations in spatial reasoning and contextual understanding.&lt;SEP&gt;Document structure processing challenges refer to difficulties systems face with complex layouts and nonlinear information flows, exposing limitations in spatial reasoning and contextual understanding.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7aefd567d430c404aab77872282400eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37ff528cd8f38cd79fa57c96fab4a7c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a908e853be8da852064e031c68c78242</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514438</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cross-Modal Misalignment">
  <data key="d0">Cross-Modal Misalignment</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Cross-Modal Misalignment is a failure scenario where all evaluated methods consistently produce incorrect answers despite having access to necessary information, suggesting fundamental limitations in handling noisy, heterogeneous multimodal data.&lt;SEP&gt;Cross-modal misalignment is a failure scenario where all evaluated methods consistently produce incorrect answers despite having access to the necessary information, revealing fundamental limitations in handling noisy, heterogeneous multimodal data.&lt;SEP&gt;Cross-modal misalignment is a failure scenario where all evaluated methods consistently produce incorrect answers despite having access to the necessary information, suggesting fundamental limitations in handling noisy, heterogeneous multimodal data.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7aefd567d430c404aab77872282400eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37ff528cd8f38cd79fa57c96fab4a7c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a908e853be8da852064e031c68c78242</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514438</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Retrieval Bias Toward Text">
  <data key="d0">Retrieval Bias Toward Text</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Retrieval Bias Toward Text is a systemic issue where RAG systems demonstrate pronounced bias toward textual passages, particularly when visual content lacks exact keyword matches, revealing weakness in cross-modal attention mechanisms.&lt;SEP&gt;Retrieval bias toward text is a systemic issue where current RAG systems demonstrate pronounced bias toward textual passages, particularly when visual content lacks exact keyword matches, even when queries explicitly instruct to prioritize visual sources.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7aefd567d430c404aab77872282400eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a908e853be8da852064e031c68c78242</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514443</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rigid Spatial Processing Patterns">
  <data key="d0">Rigid Spatial Processing Patterns</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Rigid Spatial Processing Patterns is a systemic issue where current visual processing models exhibit fundamental rigidity in spatial interpretation, defaulting to sequential processing.&lt;SEP&gt;Rigid spatial processing patterns are the fundamental rigidity in spatial interpretation exhibited by current visual processing models, which default to sequential scanning patterns.&lt;SEP&gt;Rigid spatial processing patterns are a key challenge in multimodal RAG systems, where models fail to adapt to non-standard spatial requirements such as reading a figure from bottom to top.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7aefd567d430c404aab77872282400eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18ade91e917d2c67b94279ae6220dd06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37ff528cd8f38cd79fa57c96fab4a7c2</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514438</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Multimodal RAG">
  <data key="d0">Multimodal RAG</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Multimodal RAG is a critical advancement necessary to bridge knowledge gaps and enable comprehensive intelligence across all modalities of human knowledge representation.&lt;SEP&gt;Multimodal RAG refers to retrieval-augmented generation systems that integrate multiple modalities such as text, images, tables, and equations, with current systems showing promising capabilities but fundamental limitations.&lt;SEP&gt;Multimodal RAG refers to retrieval-augmented generation systems that integrate multiple modalities, whose limitations emerge through systematic analysis of failure cases.&lt;SEP&gt;Multimodal RAG is a retrieval-augmented generation approach that handles multiple modalities such as text and images, facing challenges in cross-modal alignment and structural parsing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7aefd567d430c404aab77872282400eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a43d425aea6f4b6c0edc38f28595f400&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4b25ee421d57dc99861b0d26ac02b54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a908e853be8da852064e031c68c78242</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514433</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Multimodal Document Understanding">
  <data key="d0">Multimodal Document Understanding</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Multimodal document understanding refers to tasks that require interpreting and reasoning over documents containing multiple modalities such as text, images, tables, and equations.&lt;SEP&gt;Multimodal document understanding is an area where RAG-Anything particularly excels, according to the table results.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7aefd567d430c404aab77872282400eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49961962320a3499cad5000e71cf7f3e</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514426</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Visual Reasoning">
  <data key="d0">Visual Reasoning</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Visual reasoning is the capability to interpret and reason about visual elements such as charts, including spatial relationships between bars, axis labels, and legends.&lt;SEP&gt;Visual reasoning is the capability to interpret and analyze visual information such as charts and spatial relationships between visual elements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7aefd567d430c404aab77872282400eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-306f65a0f4295fa49788ecf8659d4b81</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514432</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bar Plot">
  <data key="d0">Bar Plot</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A bar plot is a chart type whose bars, axis labels, and legends are represented as interconnected nodes in RAG-Anything's structured graph representation.&lt;SEP&gt;A bar plot is a visual chart representation that RAG-Anything converts into a structured graph with interconnected nodes for bars, axis labels, and legends.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7aefd567d430c404aab77872282400eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-306f65a0f4295fa49788ecf8659d4b81</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514432</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AUPRC">
  <data key="d0">AUPRC</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">AUPRC is an evaluation metric used to compare model combinations, with the highest value sought for the Evidence Inference dataset.&lt;SEP&gt;AUPRC is a performance metric used to evaluate model combinations on the Evidence Inference dataset.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7aefd567d430c404aab77872282400eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89ff37f1683bc8edc5276effd3646dee</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514445</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Factual Accuracy Assessment Prompt">
  <data key="d0">Factual Accuracy Assessment Prompt</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Factual Accuracy Assessment Prompt is a standardized prompt designed for systematic factual accuracy assessment of generated responses across multiple domains, producing binary accuracy classifications with concise analytical justifications.&lt;SEP&gt;The factual accuracy assessment prompt is a standardized prompt designed for systematic factual accuracy assessment of generated responses across multiple domains, producing binary accuracy classifications with concise analytical justifications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7aefd567d430c404aab77872282400eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7eea2cc84733111d4a7fedb10d7083b8</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514427</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Context-Aware Multimodal Prompting">
  <data key="d0">Context-Aware Multimodal Prompting</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Context-Aware Multimodal Prompting is an approach using three prompts that orchestrate structured, context-aware multimodal analysis with JSON-formatted outputs to extract descriptions of visual, tabular, and mathematical content.&lt;SEP&gt;Context-aware multimodal prompting is an approach that integrates image, table, and equation analysis with surrounding text to enable contextually-grounded interpretations that enhance knowledge retrieval and substantiation.&lt;SEP&gt;Context-aware multimodal prompting is a methodology within the RAG-Anything framework that guides models to interpret images and tables using surrounding context.&lt;SEP&gt;Context-aware multimodal prompting is a methodology that ensures mathematical content becomes integral to broader argumentative frameworks, supporting enhanced retrieval accuracy, analytical traceability, and reasoning coherence.&lt;SEP&gt;Context-aware multimodal prompting is a section of the RAG-Anything framework addressing prompting strategies for multimodal contexts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7aefd567d430c404aab77872282400eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7eea2cc84733111d4a7fedb10d7083b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-840e794a234c66ff0680c138d02d19ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4b25ee421d57dc99861b0d26ac02b54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d556fb722f8eac5fc92376e70d34e60</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514426</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="LightRAG">
  <data key="d0">LightRAG</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">LightRAG is a graph-enhanced retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) system that integrates structured knowledge representation with dual-level retrieval mechanisms. It is an established text-centric extraction pipeline methodology referenced as a basis for constructing text-based knowledge graphs, and it employs a graph construction approach that uses sparsified indices to optimize structures for retrieval efficiency. As a baseline RAG framework, LightRAG is restricted to text-only content processing.

LightRAG has been evaluated on several benchmarks. On the DocBench dataset, it achieved an overall accuracy of 58.4% and led in the Law domain. On MMLongBench, it achieved an overall accuracy of 38.9%.

As a baseline model, LightRAG has also been assessed in various failure cases. It incorrectly identified VAE as having clearer separation in a multi-panel figure interpretation case, and it incorrectly answered DKK 11,503 million for Novo Nordisk's wages and salaries in 2020. It provided a partially incorrect answer regarding the lowest accuracy GCAN configuration for Twitter15, and it incorrectly identified the BERT + LSTM - Attention model with an AUPRC of 0.429 as the highest performer for the Evidence Inference dataset. In a multimodal RAG failure case, it produced an incorrect answer about the NER label generation sequence, and in a cross-modal noise case, it provided an incorrect answer regarding joint goal accuracy improvements in the Train domain.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d4727f37ea1b30518f13dc89ffc7ea1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5f0a5a74b5a4eac43772c74649ca651&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eac0008c777dab7291aec281277e77a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49961962320a3499cad5000e71cf7f3e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-306f65a0f4295fa49788ecf8659d4b81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17a576920c675eca791231767d46477b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37ff528cd8f38cd79fa57c96fab4a7c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a908e853be8da852064e031c68c78242&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1f82685779db44d104d20c4e16fe8b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89ff37f1683bc8edc5276effd3646dee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3ef854a849174a61602e3f9d4a8eac1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b8b33a1f15bc5b31bb493efd3ec933a</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514426</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MMGraphRAG">
  <data key="d0">MMGraphRAG</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">MMGraphRAG is a multimodal retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) framework that constructs unified knowledge graphs spanning both textual and visual content, employing spectral clustering for multimodal entity analysis. It links scene graphs with textual representations, though this approach has been noted to suffer from structural blindness. As a baseline RAG framework, MMGraphRAG only adds basic image processing while treating tables and equations as plain text, thereby missing crucial structural information.

MMGraphRAG has been evaluated on several benchmarks. On the DocBench dataset, it achieved an overall accuracy of 61.0%, leading in the Academia, Government, and Unanswerable categories. On MMLongBench, it achieved an overall accuracy of 37.7%.

Beyond benchmark performance, MMGraphRAG has been examined in various failure and error cases. In a multi-panel figure interpretation case, it incorrectly identified VAE as having clearer separation. It incorrectly answered 11,503 million DKK for Novo Nordisk's wages and salaries in 2020. It provided a partially incorrect answer regarding the lowest accuracy GCAN configuration for Twitter15. It incorrectly identified the Bert-To-Bert model with an AUPRC of 0.708 as the highest performer for the Evidence Inference dataset. In a multimodal RAG failure case, it produced an incorrect answer about the NER label generation sequence. In a cross-modal noise case, it provided an incorrect answer regarding joint goal accuracy improvements in the Train domain.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d4727f37ea1b30518f13dc89ffc7ea1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5f0a5a74b5a4eac43772c74649ca651&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49961962320a3499cad5000e71cf7f3e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-306f65a0f4295fa49788ecf8659d4b81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17a576920c675eca791231767d46477b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37ff528cd8f38cd79fa57c96fab4a7c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a908e853be8da852064e031c68c78242&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1f82685779db44d104d20c4e16fe8b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89ff37f1683bc8edc5276effd3646dee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3ef854a849174a61602e3f9d4a8eac1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b8b33a1f15bc5b31bb493efd3ec933a</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514428</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
