<node id="Bge-Reranker-V2-M3">
  <data key="d0">Bge-Reranker-V2-M3</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Bge-reranker-v2-m3 is a reranking model used in the retrieval pipeline.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d4727f37ea1b30518f13dc89ffc7ea1</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514165</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dual-Graph Construction Strategy">
  <data key="d0">Dual-Graph Construction Strategy</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A strategy proposed by RAG-Anything that builds a cross-modal knowledge graph and a text-based knowledge graph to avoid overlooking modality-specific structural signals.&lt;SEP&gt;The dual-graph construction strategy preserves structural relationships across all modalities and enables cross-page entity alignment.&lt;SEP&gt;The dual-graph construction strategy is RAG-Anything's core technical innovation that integrates cross-modal and text-based knowledge graphs.&lt;SEP&gt;The dual-graph construction strategy specifies the vertex set for the cross-modal knowledge graph, which is later merged with a text-based knowledge graph through entity alignment.&lt;SEP&gt;The dual-graph construction strategy is a comprehensive approach introduced by RAG-Anything that preserves structural relationships across all modalities and enables cross-page entity alignment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d4727f37ea1b30518f13dc89ffc7ea1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5f0a5a74b5a4eac43772c74649ca651&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eac0008c777dab7291aec281277e77a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1f82685779db44d104d20c4e16fe8b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-960c77c28320f020a2006dba07f70f59</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514444</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cross-Modal Hybrid Retrieval Architecture">
  <data key="d0">Cross-Modal Hybrid Retrieval Architecture</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The cross-modal hybrid retrieval architecture combines structural knowledge navigation with semantic similarity matching to leverage explicit relationships and implicit semantic connections across modalities.&lt;SEP&gt;The cross-modal hybrid retrieval architecture combines structural knowledge navigation with semantic similarity matching, enabling the framework to leverage both explicit relationships and implicit semantic connections across modalities.&lt;SEP&gt;The cross-modal hybrid retrieval architecture of RAG-Anything combines structural knowledge navigation with semantic similarity matching, enabling the framework to leverage both explicit relationships and implicit semantic connections across modalities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d4727f37ea1b30518f13dc89ffc7ea1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cb795e1c89d1938a0fcb44cbec5be74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1f82685779db44d104d20c4e16fe8b7</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514431</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Structured Context Injection Mechanism">
  <data key="d0">Structured Context Injection Mechanism</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The structured context injection mechanism integrates dual-graph construction for cross-page entity alignment and combines semantic retrieval with structural navigation.&lt;SEP&gt;The structured context injection mechanism integrates dual-graph construction for cross-page entity alignment and combines semantic retrieval with structural navigation.&lt;SEP&gt;The structured context injection mechanism is a component of RAG-Anything that integrates dual-graph construction for cross-page entity alignment and combines semantic retrieval with structural navigation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d4727f37ea1b30518f13dc89ffc7ea1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cb795e1c89d1938a0fcb44cbec5be74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1f82685779db44d104d20c4e16fe8b7</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514430</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Modality-Aware Processing">
  <data key="d0">Modality-Aware Processing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Modality-aware processing is employed for efficient context window utilization in the RAG-Anything framework.&lt;SEP&gt;Modality-aware processing is employed by RAG-Anything for efficient context window utilization.</data>
