  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Visual Content">
  <data key="d0">Visual Content</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Visual content refers to original visual artifacts recovered through dereferencing of multimodal chunks, providing rich semantics for reasoning during synthesis.&lt;SEP&gt;Visual content often contains precise, structured data such as specific numerical values, detailed diagrams, or exact spatial relationships.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d4727f37ea1b30518f13dc89ffc7ea1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18ade91e917d2c67b94279ae6220dd06</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514165</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Vision-Language Model">
  <data key="d0">Vision-Language Model</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The vision-language model jointly conditions on assembled textual context and dereferenced visual artifacts to integrate information from query, textual context, and visual content.&lt;SEP&gt;The Vision-Language Model (VLM) is a conditional generative model that produces responses by jointly conditioning on a query, textual context, and visual artifacts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d4727f37ea1b30518f13dc89ffc7ea1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e906fa59bd4a41ccc46a928ffee1aa2</data>
