<node id="Unified Multimodal Representation Challenge">
  <data key="d0">Unified Multimodal Representation Challenge</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The unified multimodal representation challenge requires seamlessly integrating diverse information types while preserving their unique characteristics and cross-modal relationships.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a43d425aea6f4b6c0edc38f28595f400</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514166</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Structure-Aware Decomposition Challenge">
  <data key="d0">Structure-Aware Decomposition Challenge</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The structure-aware decomposition challenge demands intelligent parsing of complex layouts and maintaining spatial and hierarchical relationships crucial for understanding.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a43d425aea6f4b6c0edc38f28595f400</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514166</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cross-Modal Retrieval Challenge">
  <data key="d0">Cross-Modal Retrieval Challenge</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The cross-modal retrieval challenge necessitates sophisticated mechanisms that can navigate between different modalities and reason over their interconnections during retrieval.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a43d425aea6f4b6c0edc38f28595f400</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514166</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Scientific Research">
  <data key="d0">Scientific Research</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Scientific Research is a domain where experimental results are primarily communicated through plots, diagrams, and statistical visualizations containing core discoveries invisible to text-only systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a43d425aea6f4b6c0edc38f28595f400</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514166</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Financial Analysis">
  <data key="d0">Financial Analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Financial Analysis is a domain that relies heavily on market charts, correlation matrices, and performance tables where investment insights are encoded in visual patterns.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a43d425aea6f4b6c0edc38f28595f400</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514166</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Medical Literature Analysis">
  <data key="d0">Medical Literature Analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Medical Literature Analysis is a domain that depends on radiological images, diagnostic charts, and clinical data tables containing life-critical information for diagnosis and treatment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a43d425aea6f4b6c0edc38f28595f400</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514166</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Multimodal Benchmarks">
  <data key="d0">Multimodal Benchmarks</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Multimodal benchmarks are challenging evaluation datasets on which RAG-Anything demonstrates superior performance over state-of-the-art methods.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a43d425aea6f4b6c0edc38f28595f400</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514167</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="GitHub Repository">
  <data key="d0">GitHub Repository</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The GitHub repository at https://github.com/HKUDS/RAG-Anything is where the RAG-Anything framework is open-sourced.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a43d425aea6f4b6c0edc38f28595f400</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514167</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Textual Content">
  <data key="d0">Textual Content</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Textual content is one of the modalities present in real-world knowledge repositories, alongside visual elements, structured tables, and mathematical expressions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a43d425aea6f4b6c0edc38f28595f400</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514167</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Visual Elements">
  <data key="d0">Visual Elements</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Visual elements are a modality present in real-world knowledge repositories, containing semantic richness such as charts, diagrams, and spatial layouts that cannot be adequately captured through text alone.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a43d425aea6f4b6c0edc38f28595f400</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514167</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Structured Tables">
  <data key="d0">Structured Tables</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Structured tables are a modality present in real-world knowledge repositories that carry essential meaning in document-intensive domains.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a43d425aea6f4b6c0edc38f28595f400</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514167</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mathematical Expressions">
  <data key="d0">Mathematical Expressions</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Mathematical expressions are a modality present in real-world knowledge repositories that resist meaningful conversion to plain text.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a43d425aea6f4b6c0edc38f28595f400</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514167</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Multimodal Encoders">
  <data key="d0">Multimodal Encoders</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Multimodal encoders are advanced components that can capture both intra-modal and inter-modal dependencies without losing essential visual semantics.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a43d425aea6f4b6c0edc38f28595f400</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514167</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Layout-Aware Parsing Modules">
  <data key="d0">Layout-Aware Parsing Modules</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Layout-aware parsing modules are specialized components that can interpret document structure and preserve contextual positioning of multimodal elements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a43d425aea6f4b6c0edc38f28595f400</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514167</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cross-Modal Alignment Systems">
  <data key="d0">Cross-Modal Alignment Systems</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Cross-modal alignment systems are components capable of understanding semantic correspondences across text, images, and structured data.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a43d425aea6f4b6c0edc38f28595f400</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514167</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Knowledge Graphs">
  <data key="d0">Knowledge Graphs</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Knowledge graphs are complementary structures constructed by RAG-Anything that preserve both multimodal contextual relationships and detailed textual knowledge.&lt;SEP&gt;Knowledge graphs are one of the complementary knowledge sources whose strengths are leveraged in the synthesis stage of the framework.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a43d425aea6f4b6c0edc38f28595f400&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e906fa59bd4a41ccc46a928ffee1aa2</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514436</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Multimodal Knowledge Unification">
  <data key="d0">Multimodal Knowledge Unification</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Multimodal Knowledge Unification is a process introduced by RAG-Anything that decomposes raw inputs into atomic knowledge units while preserving structural context and semantic alignment.&lt;SEP&gt;A process that provides a uniform abstraction across modalities, decomposing diverse file formats into atomic units while maintaining hierarchical order and contextual relationships.&lt;SEP&gt;Multimodal Knowledge Unification is a process formalized by Equation (1) that transforms heterogeneous documents into a unified, retrieval-oriented representation.&lt;SEP&gt;Multimodal Knowledge Unification is a process that decomposes knowledge sources into atomic content units with modality types such as text, image, table, and equation, preserving semantic integrity and structural context.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dded67fd8182de2201aa35ccbb4c8cd9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eac0008c777dab7291aec281277e77a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0efdf5167592c14e899f82452298f2ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-808bf767f815e787e09b6b3e8a122b71</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514435</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Universal Indexing">
  <data key="d0">Universal Indexing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Universal indexing is a core component of RAG-Anything that handles multimodal knowledge for retrieval.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dded67fd8182de2201aa35ccbb4c8cd9</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514167</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cross-Modal Adaptive Retrieval">
  <data key="d0">Cross-Modal Adaptive Retrieval</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Cross-modal adaptive retrieval is a core component of RAG-Anything that retrieves information across different modalities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dded67fd8182de2201aa35ccbb4c8cd9</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514167</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Knowledge-Enhanced Response Generation">
  <data key="d0">Knowledge-Enhanced Response Generation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Knowledge-enhanced response generation is a core component of RAG-Anything that generates responses using retrieved multimodal knowledge.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dded67fd8182de2201aa35ccbb4c8cd9</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514167</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Modality-Aware Query Processing">
  <data key="d0">Modality-Aware Query Processing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Modality-aware query processing is a system introduced by RAG-Anything that enables textual queries to effectively access visual and structured information.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dded67fd8182de2201aa35ccbb4c8cd9</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514167</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cross-Modal Alignment">
  <data key="d0">Cross-Modal Alignment</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Cross-modal alignment is a system introduced by RAG-Anything that aligns information across different modalities for effective retrieval.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dded67fd8182de2201aa35ccbb4c8cd9</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514167</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Multimodal Knowledge Representation">
  <data key="d0">Multimodal Knowledge Representation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Multimodal knowledge representation is a concept that RAG-Anything fundamentally reimagines, involving the unified handling of diverse data modalities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dded67fd8182de2201aa35ccbb4c8cd9</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514168</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cross-Modal Understanding">
  <data key="d0">Cross-Modal Understanding</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Cross-modal understanding refers to the ability to comprehend and reason across different modalities such as text, images, tables, and equations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dded67fd8182de2201aa35ccbb4c8cd9</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514168</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Textual Semantics">
  <data key="d0">Textual Semantics</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Textual semantics refers to the fine-grained meaning and structure of textual content, which RAG-Anything bridges with cross-modal understanding.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dded67fd8182de2201aa35ccbb4c8cd9</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514168</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Multimodal Contextual Relationships">
  <data key="d0">Multimodal Contextual Relationships</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Multimodal contextual relationships are the connections between different modalities preserved by the complementary knowledge graphs constructed by RAG-Anything.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dded67fd8182de2201aa35ccbb4c8cd9</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514168</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Semantic Integrity">
  <data key="d0">Semantic Integrity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Semantic integrity is maintained across modalities by the RAG-Anything system to ensure consistent meaning.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dded67fd8182de2201aa35ccbb4c8cd9</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514168</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cross-Modal Reasoning">
  <data key="d0">Cross-Modal Reasoning</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Cross-modal reasoning is the capability to reason across different modalities, which RAG-Anything ensures throughout the retrieval process.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dded67fd8182de2201aa35ccbb4c8cd9</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514168</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dense Vector Representations">
  <data key="d0">Dense Vector Representations</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Dense vector representations are used by RAG-Anything to identify semantically relevant content that lacks direct structural connections.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dded67fd8182de2201aa35ccbb4c8cd9</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514168</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Multi-Hop Reasoning">
  <data key="d0">Multi-Hop Reasoning</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Multi-hop reasoning refers to reasoning patterns captured through explicit graph relationships in the RAG-Anything framework.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dded67fd8182de2201aa35ccbb4c8cd9</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514168</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Embedding-Based Retrieval">
  <data key="d0">Embedding-Based Retrieval</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Embedding-based retrieval is an existing approach that relies solely on embeddings, which RAG-Anything addresses as a fundamental limitation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dded67fd8182de2201aa35ccbb4c8cd9</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514168</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Keyword Matching">
  <data key="d0">Keyword Matching</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Keyword matching is an existing retrieval approach whose limitations RAG-Anything addresses through its hybrid retrieval mechanism.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dded67fd8182de2201aa35ccbb4c8cd9</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514168</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Graph-Based Knowledge Representation">
  <data key="d0">Graph-Based Knowledge Representation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Graph-based knowledge representation is the approach that provides the primary performance gains in RAG-Anything, as revealed by ablation studies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dded67fd8182de2201aa35ccbb4c8cd9</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514168</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Chunk-Based Approaches">
  <data key="d0">Chunk-Based Approaches</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Chunk-based approaches are traditional methods that fail to capture the structural relationships critical for multimodal reasoning.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dded67fd8182de2201aa35ccbb4c8cd9</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514168</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Multimodal RAG Systems">
  <data key="d0">Multimodal RAG Systems</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Multimodal RAG systems are retrieval-augmented generation systems designed to handle multiple modalities, which suffer from architectural fragmentation that RAG-Anything eliminates.&lt;SEP&gt;Multimodal RAG systems are retrieval-augmented generation systems that handle both textual and visual information, exhibiting failure modes such as cross-modal misalignment and retrieval bias.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dded67fd8182de2201aa35ccbb4c8cd9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37ff528cd8f38cd79fa57c96fab4a7c2</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514439</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Atomic Knowledge Units">
  <data key="d0">Atomic Knowledge Units</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Atomic knowledge units are the decomposed components of raw inputs in RAG-Anything, each consisting of a modality type and corresponding raw content.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dded67fd8182de2201aa35ccbb4c8cd9</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514168</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Modality Type">
  <data key="d0">Modality Type</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Modality type refers to the category of a content unit such as text, image, table, or equation in the RAG-Anything framework.&lt;SEP&gt;Modality type t_j denotes the type of content such as text, image, table, or equation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dded67fd8182de2201aa35ccbb4c8cd9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0efdf5167592c14e899f82452298f2ca</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514435</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Specialized Parsers">
  <data key="d0">Specialized Parsers</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Specialized parsers are used by RAG-Anything for high-fidelity extraction of different content types including text, figures, tables, and mathematical expressions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dded67fd8182de2201aa35ccbb4c8cd9</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514168</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Canonicalization">
  <data key="d0">Canonicalization</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Canonicalization is the process of abstracting diverse file formats into atomic units while maintaining hierarchical order and contextual relationships, enabling uniform processing, indexing, and retrieval.&lt;SEP&gt;A process that enables uniform processing, indexing, and retrieval of multimodal content within the framework.&lt;SEP&gt;A principle embodied by the equation, ensuring all components are mapped to dense vectors using the same encoder.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dded67fd8182de2201aa35ccbb4c8cd9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eac0008c777dab7291aec281277e77a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-885744df4898cd552f1960ba1b518cb4</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514429</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Text">
  <data key="d0">Text</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Text typically provides general, conceptual descriptions that may be topically related to visual content but operate at a different granularity level.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-18ade91e917d2c67b94279ae6220dd06</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514169</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Semantic Misalignment">
  <data key="d0">Semantic Misalignment</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Semantic misalignment refers to the mismatch between precise visual data and general textual descriptions, introducing noise that misleads the reasoning process.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-18ade91e917d2c67b94279ae6220dd06</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514169</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sequential Scanning Patterns">
  <data key="d0">Sequential Scanning Patterns</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Sequential scanning patterns are top-to-bottom and left-to-right processing approaches that mirror natural reading conventions and are used by most systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-18ade91e917d2c67b94279ae6220dd06</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514169</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Structural Noise">
  <data key="d0">Structural Noise</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Structural noise refers to parsing ambiguities and misinterpretations caused by structural irregularities in documents, such as ambiguous table layouts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-18ade91e917d2c67b94279ae6220dd06</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514169</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ambiguous Table Layouts">
  <data key="d0">Ambiguous Table Layouts</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Ambiguous table layouts are structurally confusing table designs, such as those lacking dedicated cell boundaries or having merged columns, that mislead extraction algorithms.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-18ade91e917d2c67b94279ae6220dd06</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514169</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Figure 12">
  <data key="d0">Figure 12</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Figure 12 is a figure showing a structurally ambiguous table where all methods failed.&lt;SEP&gt;Figure 12 illustrates the ambiguous table structure case where all methods fail to correctly parse a confusing table layout with merged cells and unclear column boundaries.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-18ade91e917d2c67b94279ae6220dd06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a908e853be8da852064e031c68c78242</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514443</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="GEM Row">
  <data key="d0">GEM Row</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The GEM row is a row in the ambiguous table that lacks dedicated cell boundaries.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-18ade91e917d2c67b94279ae6220dd06</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514169</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Joint Column">
  <data key="d0">Joint Column</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The Joint column is a column in the ambiguous table that merges with the Slot column without clear separation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-18ade91e917d2c67b94279ae6220dd06</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514169</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Slot Column">
  <data key="d0">Slot Column</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The Slot column is a column in the ambiguous table that merges with the Joint column without clear separation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-18ade91e917d2c67b94279ae6220dd06</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514169</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="RAG Systems">
  <data key="d0">RAG Systems</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">RAG systems are retrieval-augmented generation systems that exhibit brittleness when faced with real-world document variations deviating from clean, structured formats.&lt;SEP&gt;Retrieval-augmented generation systems for which scalable, fine-grained semantic search over heterogeneous multimodal knowledge is essential.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-18ade91e917d2c67b94279ae6220dd06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-885744df4898cd552f1960ba1b518cb4</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514429</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Layout-Aware Parsing Mechanisms">
  <data key="d0">Layout-Aware Parsing Mechanisms</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Layout-aware parsing mechanisms are proposed enhancements for RAG systems that can recognize and adapt to structural irregularities rather than imposing rigid formatting assumptions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-18ade91e917d2c67b94279ae6220dd06</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514169</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Visual Processing Capabilities">
  <data key="d0">Visual Processing Capabilities</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Visual processing capabilities are proposed integrations that could improve noise resilience by leveraging spatial relationships and contextual design cues.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-18ade91e917d2c67b94279ae6220dd06</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514169</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Visual Processing Models">
  <data key="d0">Visual Processing Models</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Visual processing models are current systems that exhibit fundamental rigidity in spatial interpretation, defaulting to sequential scanning patterns.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-18ade91e917d2c67b94279ae6220dd06</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514169</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tables">
  <data key="d0">Tables</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Tables are document structures that demand column-wise interpretation rather than conventional sequential scanning.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-18ade91e917d2c67b94279ae6220dd06</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514169</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Technical Diagrams">
  <data key="d0">Technical Diagrams</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Technical diagrams are document structures that follow specific directional flows requiring non-conventional processing strategies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-18ade91e917d2c67b94279ae6220dd06</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514169</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Scientific Figures">
  <data key="d0">Scientific Figures</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Scientific figures are document structures that embed critical information in unexpectedly positioned annotations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-18ade91e917d2c67b94279ae6220dd06</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514170</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Adaptive Spatial Reasoning">
  <data key="d0">Adaptive Spatial Reasoning</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Adaptive spatial reasoning is an essential capability for handling structural variations prevalent in professional documents.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-18ade91e917d2c67b94279ae6220dd06</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514170</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Extraction Algorithms">
  <data key="d0">Extraction Algorithms</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Extraction algorithms are parsing methods that are systematically misled by structural irregularities in ambiguous table layouts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-18ade91e917d2c67b94279ae6220dd06</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514170</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Spatial Relationships">
  <data key="d0">Spatial Relationships</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Spatial relationships are contextual cues leveraged by visual models to improve noise resilience.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-18ade91e917d2c67b94279ae6220dd06</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514170</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Contextual Design Cues">
  <data key="d0">Contextual Design Cues</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Contextual design cues are visual elements that are lost in purely structural representations but can be leveraged by visual models.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-18ade91e917d2c67b94279ae6220dd06</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514170</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
