  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MM-VID">
  <data key="d0">MM-VID</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">MM-VID is a multimodal RAG method that converts videos to text, losing visual information.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f5f0a5a74b5a4eac43772c74649ca651</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514177</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="VisRAG">
  <data key="d0">VisRAG</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">VisRAG is a multimodal RAG method that preserves document layouts as images but misses granular relationships.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f5f0a5a74b5a4eac43772c74649ca651</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514177</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Multimodal Retrieval-Augmented Generation">
  <data key="d0">Multimodal Retrieval-Augmented Generation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Multimodal RAG is an evolution from text-based RAG systems that integrates external knowledge from diverse data modalities for comprehensive response generation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f5f0a5a74b5a4eac43772c74649ca651</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514177</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hybrid Retrieval Mechanism">
  <data key="d0">Hybrid Retrieval Mechanism</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The hybrid retrieval mechanism combines structural navigation with semantic matching to enable precise reasoning over complex document layouts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f5f0a5a74b5a4eac43772c74649ca651</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514177</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Architectural Fragmentation">
  <data key="d0">Architectural Fragmentation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Architectural fragmentation is the fundamental problem where current multimodal RAG systems require specialized processing pipelines for each modality, causing poor generalizability and cross-modal alignment difficulties.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f5f0a5a74b5a4eac43772c74649ca651</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514177</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rigid Spatial Processing">
  <data key="d0">Rigid Spatial Processing</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Rigid spatial processing is a limitation where systems fail to adapt to non-standard document layouts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f5f0a5a74b5a4eac43772c74649ca651</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514177</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Appendix A.5">
  <data key="d0">Appendix A.5</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Appendix A.5 is a section of the document containing analysis that reveals critical challenges facing current multimodal RAG systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f5f0a5a74b5a4eac43772c74649ca651</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
