<node id="Overall Accuracy">
  <data key="d0">Overall Accuracy</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Overall accuracy is the aggregate performance metric across all domains and types in the DocBench dataset evaluation.&lt;SEP&gt;Overall accuracy is the final evaluation metric in the ablation study, with Chunk-Only at 60.0%, W/o Reranker at 62.4%, and RAG-Anything at 63.4%.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-49961962320a3499cad5000e71cf7f3e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21f9c375189978b339552ff8ff4ba819</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514425</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Table 2">
  <data key="d0">Table 2</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Table 2 presents accuracy (%) results on the DocBench dataset, comparing four methods across domain and document type categories, with best scores highlighted in dark blue and second-best in light blue.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-49961962320a3499cad5000e71cf7f3e</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514426</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Graph Construction">
  <data key="d0">Graph Construction</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Graph construction is an architectural design choice discussed in ablation studies, shown to be essential for handling multimodal documents.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-49961962320a3499cad5000e71cf7f3e</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514426</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cross-Modal Integration">
  <data key="d0">Cross-Modal Integration</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Cross-modal integration is an architectural design choice discussed in ablation studies, shown to be essential for handling multimodal documents.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-49961962320a3499cad5000e71cf7f3e</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514426</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Figure 7">
  <data key="d0">Figure 7</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Figure 7 is a figure presenting the vision analysis prompt for context-aware image interpretation and knowledge extraction.&lt;SEP&gt;Figure 7 is a figure that orchestrates comprehensive image-context integration through the Vision Analysis Prompt.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7eea2cc84733111d4a7fedb10d7083b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-840e794a234c66ff0680c138d02d19ef</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514427</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Figure 8">
  <data key="d0">Figure 8</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Figure 8 is a figure presenting the table analysis prompt for structured content decomposition and semantic understanding.&lt;SEP&gt;Figure 8 is a figure that structures systematic tabular content decomposition through the Table Analysis Prompt.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7eea2cc84733111d4a7fedb10d7083b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-840e794a234c66ff0680c138d02d19ef</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514427</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Figure 9">
  <data key="d0">Figure 9</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Figure 9 is a figure presenting the equation analysis prompt that prioritizes semantic interpretation of mathematical expressions.&lt;SEP&gt;Figure 9 is a figure that prioritizes semantic interpretation over syntactic restatement of mathematical expressions through the Equation Analysis Prompt.&lt;SEP&gt;Figure 9 is a figure that presents the equation analysis prompt for mathematical expression interpretation and integration.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7eea2cc84733111d4a7fedb10d7083b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-840e794a234c66ff0680c138d02d19ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d556fb722f8eac5fc92376e70d34e60</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514427</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Figure 10">
  <data key="d0">Figure 10</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Figure 10 is a figure presenting the standardized prompt designed for systematic factual accuracy assessment of generated responses.&lt;SEP&gt;Figure 10 presents a standardized prompt specifically designed for systematic factual accuracy assessment of generated responses across multiple domains.&lt;SEP&gt;Figure 10 is a figure presenting the standardized accuracy evaluation prompt for consistent factual assessment across question types.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7eea2cc84733111d4a7fedb10d7083b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4b25ee421d57dc99861b0d26ac02b54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d556fb722f8eac5fc92376e70d34e60</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514427</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Table Analysis Prompt Image">
  <data key="d0">Table Analysis Prompt Image</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Table Analysis Prompt Image is a screenshot of a code editor window displaying the Table Analysis Prompt template, including a JSON structure with detailed_description and entity_info keys and placeholders for context, image path, caption, body, and footnotes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7eea2cc84733111d4a7fedb10d7083b8</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514427</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Entity Info">
  <data key="d0">Entity Info</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Entity info is a JSON key containing a nested object with entity_name, entity_type, and summary fields.&lt;SEP&gt;Entity Info is a JSON key in the Table Analysis Prompt response containing nested fields entity_name, entity_type, and summary, where entity_type is set to table and summary provides a concise summary of the table's purpose, key findings, and relationship to surrounding content.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7eea2cc84733111d4a7fedb10d7083b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-840e794a234c66ff0680c138d02d19ef</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514427</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Table">
  <data key="d0">Table</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Table is the entity_type value specified in the entity_info section of the Table Analysis Prompt, representing tabular content to be analyzed.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7eea2cc84733111d4a7fedb10d7083b8</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514427</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mathematical Equation">
  <data key="d0">Mathematical Equation</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A LaTeX-formatted equation (Equation 5) that defines the embedding table τ as the image of the embedding function emb(·) applied to all components s belonging to the union of the vertex set V, the edge set E, and the set of atomic content chunks c_j.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-885744df4898cd552f1960ba1b518cb4</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514428</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Embedding Table τ">
  <data key="d0">Embedding Table τ</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The embedding table τ is defined as the set of dense representations { emb(s) | s ∈ V ∪ E ∪ c_j }, mapping all graph components and content chunks to vectors in a shared embedding space.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-885744df4898cd552f1960ba1b518cb4</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514428</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Embedding Function Emb(·)">
  <data key="d0">Embedding Function Emb(·)</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A modality-aware encoder that maps each component to a dense vector in a shared embedding space, embodying the principle of modality-consistent representation and canonicalization.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-885744df4898cd552f1960ba1b518cb4</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514428</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Vertex Set V">
  <data key="d0">Vertex Set V</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The vertex set V denotes the entities of the unified knowledge graph G = (V, E).</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-885744df4898cd552f1960ba1b518cb4</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514428</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Edge Set E">
  <data key="d0">Edge Set E</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The edge set E denotes the relations of the unified knowledge graph G = (V, E).</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-885744df4898cd552f1960ba1b518cb4</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514428</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Atomic Content Chunks c_j">
  <data key="d0">Atomic Content Chunks c_j</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The set c_j represents atomic content chunks extracted from multimodal documents including text, figures, tables, and equations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-885744df4898cd552f1960ba1b518cb4</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514428</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Unified Knowledge Graph G">
  <data key="d0">Unified Knowledge Graph G</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The unified knowledge graph G = (V, E) is formed by fusing the cross-modal knowledge graph and the text-based knowledge graph via entity alignment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-885744df4898cd552f1960ba1b518cb4</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514428</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Retrieval Index T">
  <data key="d0">Retrieval Index T</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The complete retrieval index T = (G, τ), consisting of the unified knowledge graph G and the embedding table τ.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-885744df4898cd552f1960ba1b518cb4</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514428</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hybrid Retrieval Architecture">
  <data key="d0">Hybrid Retrieval Architecture</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The hybrid retrieval architecture is a component of RAG-Anything that addresses the long-context challenge posed by documents with high average token counts.&lt;SEP&gt;An architecture supporting both structural knowledge navigation and semantic similarity matching, enabled by the union over V, E, and c_j.&lt;SEP&gt;The hybrid retrieval architecture combines structural navigation and semantic similarity to yield a unified candidate pool.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-885744df4898cd552f1960ba1b518cb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e906fa59bd4a41ccc46a928ffee1aa2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5eb0987c79c221cedef1a930b87f821f</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514429</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Modality-Consistent Representation">
  <data key="d0">Modality-Consistent Representation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The principle that all components, regardless of original modality, are mapped to dense vectors using the same encoder.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-885744df4898cd552f1960ba1b518cb4</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514429</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Shared Embedding Space">
  <data key="d0">Shared Embedding Space</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A unified vector space in which the embedding function emb(·) maps each component to a dense vector, enabling comparison of queries and knowledge components.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-885744df4898cd552f1960ba1b518cb4</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514429</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Scalable Fine-Grained Semantic Search">
  <data key="d0">Scalable Fine-Grained Semantic Search</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A practical capability enabled by the equation, allowing semantic search over heterogeneous multimodal knowledge.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-885744df4898cd552f1960ba1b518cb4</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514429</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Heterogeneous Multimodal Knowledge">
  <data key="d0">Heterogeneous Multimodal Knowledge</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Knowledge spanning multiple modalities that the equation enables scalable, fine-grained semantic search over.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-885744df4898cd552f1960ba1b518cb4</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514430</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="JSON Schema">
  <data key="d0">JSON Schema</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The JSON schema is a structure defined in the prompt with two top-level keys, detailed_description and entity_info, where entity_info contains entity_name, entity_type, and summary.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-840e794a234c66ff0680c138d02d19ef</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514430</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
