</node>
<node id="DocBench QA Counts">
  <data key="d0">DocBench QA Counts</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">DocBench QA Counts is a vertical bar chart visualizing the distribution of question-answer pairs across different document length categories, showing that the majority of QA pairs are concentrated in shorter documents (1-50 pages) with a sharp decline for longer documents.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8cb795e1c89d1938a0fcb44cbec5be74</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514431</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Semantic Retrieval">
  <data key="d0">Semantic Retrieval</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Semantic retrieval is a technique combined with structural navigation within the structured context injection mechanism of RAG-Anything.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8cb795e1c89d1938a0fcb44cbec5be74</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514431</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Structural Navigation">
  <data key="d0">Structural Navigation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Structural navigation is a technique combined with semantic retrieval within the structured context injection mechanism of RAG-Anything.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8cb795e1c89d1938a0fcb44cbec5be74</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514431</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Twitter16">
  <data key="d0">Twitter16</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Twitter16 is a dataset used to evaluate the accuracy of GCAN sub-model configurations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-306f65a0f4295fa49788ecf8659d4b81</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514432</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Figure 5">
  <data key="d0">Figure 5</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Figure 5 is a visual reasoning case illustration showing how RAG-Anything handles complex chart interpretation tasks.&lt;SEP&gt;Figure 5 illustrates how RAG-Anything handles complex visual reasoning tasks involving chart interpretation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-306f65a0f4295fa49788ecf8659d4b81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89ff37f1683bc8edc5276effd3646dee</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514432</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="-S-A">
  <data key="d0">-S-A</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">-S-A is a GCAN model configuration involving the removal of source tweet embeddings and dual co-attention, which resulted in the lowest accuracy for Twitter15.&lt;SEP&gt;-S-A is a GCAN submodel component whose removal (source tweet embeddings and dual co-attention) yields the lowest accuracy on Twitter15.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-306f65a0f4295fa49788ecf8659d4b81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89ff37f1683bc8edc5276effd3646dee</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514432</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Multimodal Document">
  <data key="d0">Multimodal Document</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A multimodal document contains rich structural information within each modality, and understanding intra-modal structures is crucial for accurate reasoning.&lt;SEP&gt;A multimodal document is a document containing rich structural information across multiple modalities, such as text, figures, and tables.&lt;SEP&gt;A multimodal document is a source document containing both visual and textual elements, used as input for visual reasoning tasks.&lt;SEP&gt;The multimodal document is a page from a research paper containing an evidence figure that shows the NER label generation sequence in reverse order from bottom to top.&lt;SEP&gt;The multimodal document is a page containing text and Figure 2, which is referenced in the cross-modal noise case question about model style space separation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-306f65a0f4295fa49788ecf8659d4b81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17a576920c675eca791231767d46477b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37ff528cd8f38cd79fa57c96fab4a7c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a908e853be8da852064e031c68c78242&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3ef854a849174a61602e3f9d4a8eac1</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514432</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Graph Representation">
  <data key="d0">Graph Representation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Graph representation is a technique used by RAG-Anything to construct structured graphs of visual elements, linking them through semantic relations like bar-of and label-applies-to.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-306f65a0f4295fa49788ecf8659d4b81</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514432</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mathematical Equation Analysis">
  <data key="d0">Mathematical Equation Analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Mathematical Equation Analysis refers to the examination of Equation (3), which defines the vertex set of the cross-modal knowledge graph constructed by RAG-Anything.&lt;SEP&gt;A mathematical analysis describing Equation (4), which defines the edge set of a cross-modal knowledge graph constructed by RAG-Anything.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0238e7dae37f77eecdb2fe491a026dc0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-960c77c28320f020a2006dba07f70f59</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514432</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Equation (4)">
  <data key="d0">Equation (4)</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Equation (4) is a LaTeX-formatted mathematical equation defining the edge set $\tilde{E}$ as a union of intra-chunk relation sets and explicit 'belongs_to' edges.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0238e7dae37f77eecdb2fe491a026dc0</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514432</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Edge Set $\tilde{E}$">
  <data key="d0">Edge Set $\tilde{E}$</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The edge set $\tilde{E}$ is defined by Equation (4) as the union of all intra-chunk relation sets and explicit 'belongs_to' edges anchoring intra-chunk entities to multimodal entity nodes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0238e7dae37f77eecdb2fe491a026dc0</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514433</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Intra-Chunk Relation Sets $\bigcup_j \mathcal{E}_j$">
  <data key="d0">Intra-Chunk Relation Sets $\bigcup_j \mathcal{E}_j$</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The collection of all intra-chunk relation sets extracted from each non-text atomic unit via the graph extraction routine applied to its description.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0238e7dae37f77eecdb2fe491a026dc0</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514433</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Non-Text Atomic Unit $c_j$">
  <data key="d0">Non-Text Atomic Unit $c_j$</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">A non-text atomic unit from which intra-chunk relation sets and entities are extracted via the graph extraction routine.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0238e7dae37f77eecdb2fe491a026dc0</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514433</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Graph Extraction Routine $R(\cdot)$">
  <data key="d0">Graph Extraction Routine $R(\cdot)$</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A routine applied to the description of a non-text atomic unit to extract intra-chunk relation sets and entities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0238e7dae37f77eecdb2fe491a026dc0</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514433</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Intra-Chunk Entities $\mathcal{V}_j$">
  <data key="d0">Intra-Chunk Entities $\mathcal{V}_j$</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The set of entities extracted from a non-text atomic unit's textual description, which are linked to the multimodal entity node via 'belongs_to' edges.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0238e7dae37f77eecdb2fe491a026dc0</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514433</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Multimodal Entity Node $v_j^{\mathrm{mm}}$">
  <data key="d0">Multimodal Entity Node $v_j^{\mathrm{mm}}$</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">An anchor node representing non-textual content, to which all entities extracted from a unit's textual description are explicitly linked.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0238e7dae37f77eecdb2fe491a026dc0</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514433</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Unified Graph $\mathcal{G} = (\mathcal{V}, \mathcal{E})$">
  <data key="d0">Unified Graph $\mathcal{G} = (\mathcal{V}, \mathcal{E})$</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The unified graph formed by merging the edge set $\tilde{E}$ with the text-based knowledge graph through entity alignment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0238e7dae37f77eecdb2fe491a026dc0</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514433</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Description $d_j^{\mathrm{chunk}}$">
  <data key="d0">Description $d_j^{\mathrm{chunk}}$</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The textual description of a non-text atomic unit, to which the graph extraction routine is applied to extract intra-chunk relation sets and entities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0238e7dae37f77eecdb2fe491a026dc0</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514433</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Union Over All Non-Text Atomic Units $\bigcup_j$">
  <data key="d0">Union Over All Non-Text Atomic Units $\bigcup_j$</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The symbol denoting the union over all non-text atomic units $j$ in Equation (4).</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0238e7dae37f77eecdb2fe491a026dc0</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514433</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Accuracy Evaluation Prompt">
  <data key="d0">Accuracy Evaluation Prompt</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Accuracy Evaluation Prompt is a standardized prompt template designed for systematic factual accuracy assessment of generated responses across multiple domains, establishing explicit evaluation criteria that prioritize content correctness over stylistic considerations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b4b25ee421d57dc99861b0d26ac02b54</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514433</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Accuracy Evaluation">
  <data key="d0">Accuracy Evaluation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Accuracy evaluation is a systematic assessment process producing binary accuracy classifications accompanied by concise analytical justifications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b4b25ee421d57dc99861b0d26ac02b54</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514433</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Failure Patterns">
  <data key="d0">Failure Patterns</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Failure patterns are two critical patterns revealed by investigation that expose deeper systemic issues in multimodal RAG architectures, reflecting fundamental challenges in cross-modal information integration and structural reasoning.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b4b25ee421d57dc99861b0d26ac02b54</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514433</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cross-Modal Information Integration">
  <data key="d0">Cross-Modal Information Integration</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Cross-modal information integration is a fundamental challenge in multimodal RAG architectures identified through failure pattern analysis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b4b25ee421d57dc99861b0d26ac02b54</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514434</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Structural Reasoning">
  <data key="d0">Structural Reasoning</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Structural reasoning is a fundamental challenge in multimodal RAG architectures identified through failure pattern analysis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b4b25ee421d57dc99861b0d26ac02b54</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514434</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Binary Accuracy Classification">
  <data key="d0">Binary Accuracy Classification</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Binary accuracy classification is the scoring system used in the accuracy evaluation prompt, assigning a score of 0 or 1.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b4b25ee421d57dc99861b0d26ac02b54</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514434</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="JSON Output Format">
  <data key="d0">JSON Output Format</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The JSON output format is the specification requiring an output object with 'accuracy' and 'reasoning' fields.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b4b25ee421d57dc99861b0d26ac02b54</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514434</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
