  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Equation (1)">
  <data key="d0">Equation (1)</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Equation (1) is a LaTeX-formatted mathematical equation that formalizes the Multimodal Knowledge Unification process, stating that each knowledge source k_i from corpus K is decomposed into a set of n_i atomic content units {c_j}, where each unit c_j is a pair (t_j, x_j).</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0efdf5167592c14e899f82452298f2ca</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514434</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="RAG-Anything Framework">
  <data key="d0">RAG-Anything Framework</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The RAG-Anything framework is a system in which Equation (1) formalizes the Multimodal Knowledge Unification process.&lt;SEP&gt;The RAG-Anything framework is a system for cross-modal knowledge graph construction that transforms heterogeneous multimodal content into structured, retrievable knowledge.&lt;SEP&gt;The RAG-Anything framework is a multimodal retrieval-augmented generation system that defines the final response generation step through a mathematical equation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0efdf5167592c14e899f82452298f2ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e906fa59bd4a41ccc46a928ffee1aa2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93e73b1153bf931b315a02bf890fff6d</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514435</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Knowledge Source">
  <data key="d0">Knowledge Source</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">A knowledge source k_i is an element of the corpus K that is decomposed into a set of n_i atomic content units.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0efdf5167592c14e899f82452298f2ca</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514435</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Atomic Content Unit">
  <data key="d0">Atomic Content Unit</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">An atomic content unit c_j is a pair (t_j, x_j) produced by decomposing a knowledge source, where t_j denotes the modality type and x_j represents the corresponding raw content.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0efdf5167592c14e899f82452298f2ca</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514435</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Raw Content">
  <data key="d0">Raw Content</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Raw content x_j represents the content extracted in a modality-aware manner corresponding to a modality type.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0efdf5167592c14e899f82452298f2ca</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514435</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Decompose">
  <data key="d0">Decompose</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Decompose is the operation denoted by the arrow in Equation (1) that breaks each knowledge source into atomic content units.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0efdf5167592c14e899f82452298f2ca</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514435</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cross-Modal Retrieval">
  <data key="d0">Cross-Modal Retrieval</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Cross-modal retrieval is a capability supported by the canonical decomposition defined in Equation (1), enabling retrieval and reasoning across different modalities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0efdf5167592c14e899f82452298f2ca</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514435</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Corpus">
  <data key="d0">Corpus</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The corpus K is the collection of knowledge sources from which atomic content units are derived.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0efdf5167592c14e899f82452298f2ca</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514435</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="LaTeX">
  <data key="d0">LaTeX</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">LaTeX is the format used for Equation (1), a typesetting system for mathematical notation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0efdf5167592c14e899f82452298f2ca</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514435</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Modality-Aware Extraction">
  <data key="d0">Modality-Aware Extraction</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Modality-aware extraction is the manner in which raw content x_j is extracted, respecting the specific characteristics of each modality.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0efdf5167592c14e899f82452298f2ca</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514435</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Unified Multimodal Representation">
  <data key="d0">Unified Multimodal Representation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Unified multimodal representation is the challenge directly addressed by Equation (1), which defines a canonical decomposition supporting cross-modal retrieval and reasoning.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0efdf5167592c14e899f82452298f2ca</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514435</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Uniform Indexing And Retrieval">
  <data key="d0">Uniform Indexing And Retrieval</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Uniform indexing and retrieval is the process to which atomic content units are amenable, ensuring each unit retains its modality-specific characteristics.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0efdf5167592c14e899f82452298f2ca</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514435</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Query Q">
  <data key="d0">Query Q</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The query q is the original input question that the Vision-Language Model conditions on when generating a response.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1e906fa59bd4a41ccc46a928ffee1aa2</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514435</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Textual Context P(q)">
  <data key="d0">Textual Context P(q)</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The textual context P(q) is constructed by concatenating textual representations of top-ranked retrieval candidates, including entity summaries, relationship descriptions, and chunk contents, with delimiters indicating modality and hierarchy.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1e906fa59bd4a41ccc46a928ffee1aa2</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514436</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Visual Artifacts V*(q)">
  <data key="d0">Visual Artifacts V*(q)</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The visual artifacts V*(q) are a set of dereferenced visual content recovered from multimodal chunks, ensuring authentic visual semantics are available for reasoning.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1e906fa59bd4a41ccc46a928ffee1aa2</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514436</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Retrieval-to-Synthesis Pipeline">
  <data key="d0">Retrieval-to-Synthesis Pipeline</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The retrieval-to-synthesis pipeline is the overall process where hybrid retrieval yields a candidate pool that is fused and ranked, culminating in the synthesis stage that generates responses.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1e906fa59bd4a41ccc46a928ffee1aa2</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514436</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dense Representations">
  <data key="d0">Dense Representations</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Dense representations are one of the complementary knowledge sources whose strengths are leveraged in the synthesis stage of the framework.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1e906fa59bd4a41ccc46a928ffee1aa2</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514436</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="C*(q)">
  <data key="d0">C*(q)</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">C*(q) is the set of top-ranked retrieval candidates produced by fusing and ranking the unified candidate pool, whose textual representations are concatenated to form the textual context P(q).</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1e906fa59bd4a41ccc46a928ffee1aa2</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514436</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Multimodal Chunks">
  <data key="d0">Multimodal Chunks</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Multimodal chunks are retrieval units corresponding to visual artifacts that are dereferenced to recover the visual content V*(q).</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1e906fa59bd4a41ccc46a928ffee1aa2</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514436</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
