  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Question density per document in DocBench varies widely, with Financial documents having the highest density (approximately 7.2 questions per document) and Government and News documents having the lowest (approximately 3.4).</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8cdd68412adb670ecbcf365fd5720250</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514445</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Long-Document Reasoning">
  <data key="d0">Long-Document Reasoning</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Long-document reasoning is a task category in which RAG-Anything demonstrates particularly strong performance, especially as document length grows.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-162b82c942fb3baf527c7b1adf1ed920</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514445</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MMLongBench Accuracy Chart">
  <data key="d0">MMLongBench Accuracy Chart</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The MMLongBench Accuracy chart is a line chart comparing the accuracy of RAG-Anything and MM-GraphRAG across document page ranges from 1-10 to 200+, showing RAG-Anything consistently outperforming MM-GraphRAG.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-162b82c942fb3baf527c7b1adf1ed920</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514445</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="GloVe + LSTM - Attention">
  <data key="d0">GloVe + LSTM - Attention</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">GloVe + LSTM - Attention is a model combination achieving the highest AUPRC value of 0.506 for the Evidence Inference dataset.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-89ff37f1683bc8edc5276effd3646dee</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514445</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Figure 6">
  <data key="d0">Figure 6</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Figure 6 is a composite figure illustrating a tabular navigation case study for the RAG-Anything framework, showing a source document and model output comparisons.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-89ff37f1683bc8edc5276effd3646dee</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514445</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="BERT + LSTM - Attention">
  <data key="d0">BERT + LSTM - Attention</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">BERT + LSTM - Attention is a model combination with an AUPRC value of 0.429 for the Evidence Inference dataset.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-89ff37f1683bc8edc5276effd3646dee</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514445</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="BERT-to-BERT">
  <data key="d0">BERT-to-BERT</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">BERT-to-BERT is a model combination with an AUPRC value of 0.455 for the Evidence Inference dataset.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-89ff37f1683bc8edc5276effd3646dee</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514445</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bert-To-Bert">
  <data key="d0">Bert-To-Bert</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Bert-To-Bert is a model combination with an AUPRC score of 0.708 for the Evidence Inference dataset.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-89ff37f1683bc8edc5276effd3646dee</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="GloVe + LSTM - Gradient">
  <data key="d0">GloVe + LSTM - Gradient</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">GloVe + LSTM - Gradient is a model combination listed in the Evidence Inference dataset table with its respective performance metrics.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-89ff37f1683bc8edc5276effd3646dee</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="GloVe + LSTM - Line">
  <data key="d0">GloVe + LSTM - Line</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">GloVe + LSTM - Line is a model combination listed in the Evidence Inference dataset table with its respective performance metrics.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-89ff37f1683bc8edc5276effd3646dee</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="GloVe + LSTM - Random">
  <data key="d0">GloVe + LSTM - Random</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">GloVe + LSTM - Random is a model combination listed in the Evidence Inference dataset table with its respective performance metrics.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-89ff37f1683bc8edc5276effd3646dee</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="A.2 Additional Case Studies">
  <data key="d0">A.2 Additional Case Studies</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A.2 Additional Case Studies is a section heading in the RAG-Anything document containing case studies on visual reasoning and tabular navigation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-89ff37f1683bc8edc5276effd3646dee</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Equation (3)">
  <data key="d0">Equation (3)</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Equation (3) is a LaTeX-formatted mathematical equation that defines the vertex set of the cross-modal knowledge graph as the union of multimodal entity nodes and intra-chunk entity sets.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-960c77c28320f020a2006dba07f70f59</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Vertex Set">
  <data key="d0">Vertex Set</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The vertex set, denoted by \tilde{V}, is the complete set of vertices in the cross-modal knowledge graph, formed as the union of multimodal entity nodes and intra-chunk entity sets.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-960c77c28320f020a2006dba07f70f59</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Multimodal Entity Nodes">
  <data key="d0">Multimodal Entity Nodes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Multimodal entity nodes, denoted as {v_j^{mm}}_j, are anchor nodes each associated with a non-text atomic unit c_j such as an image, table, or equation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-960c77c28320f020a2006dba07f70f59</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Anchor Nodes">
  <data key="d0">Anchor Nodes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Anchor nodes v_j^{mm} are explicit multimodal entities that ground non-text content and serve as anchors in the cross-modal knowledge graph.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-960c77c28320f020a2006dba07f70f59</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Intra-Chunk Entity Sets">
  <data key="d0">Intra-Chunk Entity Sets</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Intra-chunk entity sets, denoted as \mathcal{V}_j, are fine-grained entities extracted from the textual description d_j^{chunk} of each non-text unit via the graph extraction routine R(·).</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-960c77c28320f020a2006dba07f70f59</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Non-Text Atomic Unit">
  <data key="d0">Non-Text Atomic Unit</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A non-text atomic unit c_j is a content element such as an image, table, or equation, each associated with an anchor node and a textual description.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-960c77c28320f020a2006dba07f70f59</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Textual Description">
  <data key="d0">Textual Description</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The textual description d_j^{chunk} is the generated text describing each non-text unit, from which intra-chunk entities are extracted.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-960c77c28320f020a2006dba07f70f59</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Set-Theoretic Union Operation">
  <data key="d0">Set-Theoretic Union Operation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The set-theoretic union operation combines the anchor nodes with all fine-grained entities identified within each non-text chunk to form the complete vertex set.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-960c77c28320f020a2006dba07f70f59</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Belongs_to Edges">
  <data key="d0">Belongs_to Edges</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Belongs_to edges connect each anchor node to its associated intra-chunk entities, preserving modality-specific grounding.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-960c77c28320f020a2006dba07f70f59</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514447</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Indexing">
  <data key="d0">Indexing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Indexing is a subsequent stage following graph fusion in the framework's pipeline.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-960c77c28320f020a2006dba07f70f59</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514447</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hybrid Retrieval">
  <data key="d0">Hybrid Retrieval</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Hybrid retrieval is a subsequent stage that leverages the unified graph structure for cross-modal retrieval and reasoning.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-960c77c28320f020a2006dba07f70f59</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514447</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Document Collection">
  <data key="d0">Document Collection</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The document collection is the set of documents over which the index j ranges, containing all non-text atomic units.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-960c77c28320f020a2006dba07f70f59</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514447</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Modality-Specific Grounding">
  <data key="d0">Modality-Specific Grounding</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Modality-specific grounding is preserved by the belongs_to edges connecting each anchor node to its associated intra-chunk entities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-960c77c28320f020a2006dba07f70f59</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514447</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cross-Modal Retrieval And Reasoning">
  <data key="d0">Cross-Modal Retrieval And Reasoning</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Cross-modal retrieval and reasoning is enabled by the construction that contextualizes non-textual content by its textual neighborhood.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-960c77c28320f020a2006dba07f70f59</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514447</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cross-Modal Hybrid Retrieval Mechanism">
  <data key="d0">Cross-Modal Hybrid Retrieval Mechanism</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Cross-modal hybrid retrieval is a mechanism used by RAG-Anything that is particularly effective for long-document reasoning tasks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-301da515d50a3a0d178c0683bee24465</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514447</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="QA Pair Count">
  <data key="d0">QA Pair Count</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">QA Pair Count is the y-axis of Figure 2, ranging from 0 to 700, showing the number of QA pairs per document length category.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-301da515d50a3a0d178c0683bee24465</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514447</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Long-Document Reasoning Tasks">
  <data key="d0">Long-Document Reasoning Tasks</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Long-document reasoning tasks are tasks that RAG-Anything's dual-graph construction and cross-modal hybrid retrieval mechanism are particularly effective for.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-301da515d50a3a0d178c0683bee24465</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514447</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Graph Extraction Operation">
  <data key="d0">Graph Extraction Operation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The graph extraction operation is defined by the equation (𝒱_j, ℰ_j) = R(d_j^{chunk}) and produces sets of intra-chunk entities and relations from non-text content units.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-93e73b1153bf931b315a02bf890fff6d</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514447</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Equation (𝒱_j, ℰ_j) = R(d_j^{chunk})">
  <data key="d0">Equation (𝒱_j, ℰ_j) = R(d_j^{chunk})</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The equation defines the core graph extraction operation, specifying that a routine R(·) processes a unit's description d_j^{chunk} to produce entity set 𝒱_j and relation set ℰ_j.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-93e73b1153bf931b315a02bf890fff6d</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514447</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Non-Text Atomic Content Unit">
  <data key="d0">Non-Text Atomic Content Unit</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A non-text atomic content unit c_j is an individual piece of content such as an image, table, or equation that is processed for graph extraction.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-93e73b1153bf931b315a02bf890fff6d</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514447</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Description d_j^{chunk}">
  <data key="d0">Description d_j^{chunk}</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The description d_j^{chunk} is a textual representation generated by a multimodal large language model, optimized for cross-modal retrieval and computed using the unit's local neighborhood.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-93e73b1153bf931b315a02bf890fff6d</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514447</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Relations ℰ_j">
  <data key="d0">Relations ℰ_j</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Relations ℰ_j are the set of relations among entities extracted from a non-text content unit's description.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-93e73b1153bf931b315a02bf890fff6d</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514448</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Extraction Routine R(·)">
  <data key="d0">Extraction Routine R(·)</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The extraction routine R(·) performs entity and relation extraction on the derived description of a non-text unit, analogous to named entity recognition and relation extraction in text-based pipelines.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-93e73b1153bf931b315a02bf890fff6d</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514448</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Multimodal Large Language Model">
  <data key="d0">Multimodal Large Language Model</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The multimodal large language model generates the textual description d_j^{chunk} for non-text content units.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-93e73b1153bf931b315a02bf890fff6d</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514448</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Local Neighborhood C_j">
  <data key="d0">Local Neighborhood C_j</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The local neighborhood C_j = {c_k : |k - j| ≤ δ} is the context used to compute the description, where δ controls the contextual window size.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-93e73b1153bf931b315a02bf890fff6d</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514448</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Multimodal Entity Node v_j^{mm}">
  <data key="d0">Multimodal Entity Node v_j^{mm}</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The multimodal entity node v_j^{mm} anchors the extracted entities and relations via belongs_to edges, grounding non-textual content within its textual context.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-93e73b1153bf931b315a02bf890fff6d</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514448</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Unified Knowledge Representation 𝒢 = (𝒱, ℰ)">
  <data key="d0">Unified Knowledge Representation 𝒢 = (𝒱, ℰ)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The unified knowledge representation 𝒢 = (𝒱, ℰ) is formed by fusing the cross-modal and text-based knowledge graphs through entity alignment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-93e73b1153bf931b315a02bf890fff6d</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514448</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dense Vector Space">
  <data key="d0">Dense Vector Space</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The dense vector space is where extracted entities, relations, and atomic content chunks are embedded to enable efficient similarity-based retrieval.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-93e73b1153bf931b315a02bf890fff6d</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514448</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Text-Only RAG Systems">
  <data key="d0">Text-Only RAG Systems</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Text-only RAG systems are limited by their inability to handle heterogeneous multimodal content, a limitation addressed by the RAG-Anything framework.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-93e73b1153bf931b315a02bf890fff6d</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514448</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Similarity-Based Retrieval">
  <data key="d0">Similarity-Based Retrieval</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Similarity-based retrieval is the efficient retrieval enabled by embedding extracted entities, relations, and atomic content chunks into a dense vector space.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-93e73b1153bf931b315a02bf890fff6d</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514448</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Atomic Content Chunks">
  <data key="d0">Atomic Content Chunks</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Atomic content chunks are the individual content units that, along with extracted entities and relations, are embedded into a dense vector space.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-93e73b1153bf931b315a02bf890fff6d</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514448</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Modality-Aware Graph">
  <data key="d0">Modality-Aware Graph</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A modality-aware graph is constructed by RAG-Anything to preserve essential relationships such as table header-cell-unit edges and panel-caption-axis edges.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a3ef854a849174a61602e3f9d4a8eac1</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514448</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Case 1: Multi-Panel Figure Interpretation">
  <data key="d0">Case 1: Multi-Panel Figure Interpretation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Case 1 examines a scenario in academic literature where researchers compare results across experimental conditions presented in multi-panel visualizations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a3ef854a849174a61602e3f9d4a8eac1</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514448</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Case 2: Financial Table Navigation">
  <data key="d0">Case 2: Financial Table Navigation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Case 2 addresses a challenge in financial document analysis where analysts must extract specific metrics from tables with similar terminology and multiple time periods.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a3ef854a849174a61602e3f9d4a8eac1</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514449</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Style-Space Panel">
  <data key="d0">Style-Space Panel</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The style-space panel is a subpanel in Figure 3 that shows cluster separation patterns and is the focus for comparing cluster separation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a3ef854a849174a61602e3f9d4a8eac1</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514449</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Content-Space Panel">
  <data key="d0">Content-Space Panel</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The content-space panel is an adjacent subpanel in Figure 3 that shows less clear distinctions and can cause confusion.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a3ef854a849174a61602e3f9d4a8eac1</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791514449</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
