<edge source="RAG-Anything" target="Dual-Graph Construction">
  <data key="d7">7.0</data>
  <data key="d8">RAG-Anything employs a dual-graph construction strategy to bridge cross-modal understanding and textual semantics.&lt;SEP&gt;RAG-Anything employs dual-graph construction to bridge cross-modal understanding and fine-grained textual semantics.&lt;SEP&gt;RAG-Anything fundamentally differs from existing methods through its dual-graph construction.&lt;SEP&gt;RAG-Anything employs Dual-Graph Construction to build cross-modal and text-based knowledge graphs.&lt;SEP&gt;RAG-Anything employs dual-graph construction as part of its framework.&lt;SEP&gt;RAG-Anything uses dual-graph construction as part of its framework.&lt;SEP&gt;The effectiveness of dual-graph construction is validated by the ablation study results.</data>
  <data key="d9">architectural component,effectiveness,framework component,framework design,graph strategy,knowledge representation,method component,method design,methodology</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-de93d4b6f02e5ae737b9b9e8142401cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a43d425aea6f4b6c0edc38f28595f400&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dded67fd8182de2201aa35ccbb4c8cd9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-808bf767f815e787e09b6b3e8a122b71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-162b82c942fb3baf527c7b1adf1ed920&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-301da515d50a3a0d178c0683bee24465&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21f9c375189978b339552ff8ff4ba819</data>
  <data key="d11">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1791514495</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="RAG-Anything" target="MM-GraphRAG">
  <data key="d7">4.0</data>
  <data key="d8">RAG-Anything and MM-GraphRAG exhibit comparable performance on shorter documents, but RAG-Anything's advantages grow with document length.&lt;SEP&gt;RAG-Anything and MM-GraphRAG exhibit comparable performance on shorter documents, but RAG-Anything's advantages become increasingly pronounced as document length grows.&lt;SEP&gt;RAG-Anything and MM-GraphRAG are compared on DocBench and MMLongBench, with RAG-Anything showing increasingly superior performance as document length grows.&lt;SEP&gt;RAG-Anything and MM-GraphRAG have comparable performance on shorter documents, but RAG-Anything's advantages grow with document length.</data>
  <data key="d9">benchmark evaluation,performance comparison</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-de93d4b6f02e5ae737b9b9e8142401cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cb795e1c89d1938a0fcb44cbec5be74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-162b82c942fb3baf527c7b1adf1ed920&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-301da515d50a3a0d178c0683bee24465</data>
  <data key="d11">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1791514463</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="RAG-Anything" target="DocBench">
  <data key="d7">9.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relation between RAG-Anything and DocBench centers on the evaluation of the RAG-Anything framework using the DocBench benchmark. DocBench serves as one of the benchmarks employed to assess RAG-Anything, specifically for multimodal document question answering, and it is also used in an ablation study of the framework. Beyond standard evaluation, two representative cases from DocBench are analyzed to demonstrate how RAG-Anything leverages structural information.

A key reported result is that RAG-Anything achieves over 13 points higher performance than MM-GraphRAG on DocBench for documents exceeding 100 pages. This performance gap over MM-GraphRAG is described as expanding dramatically to more than 13 points for such long documents. Overall, these evaluations on DocBench are used to validate the effectiveness of RAG-Anything.</data>
  <data key="d9">benchmark analysis,benchmark evaluation,benchmark performance,benchmarking,case study,evaluation,experimental validation,framework assessment,model evaluation,performance gap,performance measurement</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-de93d4b6f02e5ae737b9b9e8142401cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d4727f37ea1b30518f13dc89ffc7ea1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dded67fd8182de2201aa35ccbb4c8cd9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cb795e1c89d1938a0fcb44cbec5be74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5eb0987c79c221cedef1a930b87f821f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1f82685779db44d104d20c4e16fe8b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-162b82c942fb3baf527c7b1adf1ed920&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3ef854a849174a61602e3f9d4a8eac1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21f9c375189978b339552ff8ff4ba819</data>
  <data key="d11">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1791514466</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="RAG-Anything" target="MMLongBench">
  <data key="d7">8.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relation between MMLongBench and RAG-Anything is that of a benchmark and the framework evaluated on it. MMLongBench serves as one of the benchmarks used to assess the RAG-Anything framework, specifically for long-context multimodal document comprehension. Through evaluation on MMLongBench, RAG-Anything's effectiveness is validated. The framework demonstrates consistent accuracy improvements across all length categories on this benchmark, and it achieves the best results in information-dense domains, such as Research Reports and Financial Reports.</data>
  <data key="d9">benchmark evaluation,benchmark performance,benchmarking,evaluation,experimental validation,framework assessment,model evaluation,performance measurement,superior performance</data>
  <data key="d10">chunk-de93d4b6f02e5ae737b9b9e8142401cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d4727f37ea1b30518f13dc89ffc7ea1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dded67fd8182de2201aa35ccbb4c8cd9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cb795e1c89d1938a0fcb44cbec5be74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5eb0987c79c221cedef1a930b87f821f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1f82685779db44d104d20c4e16fe8b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-162b82c942fb3baf527c7b1adf1ed920&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-301da515d50a3a0d178c0683bee24465</data>
  <data key="d11">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1791514465</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="RAG-Anything" target="Chunk-Only">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The chunk-only variant of RAG-Anything achieves merely 60.0% accuracy, demonstrating that graph construction is essential.</data>
  <data key="d9">ablation study,architectural validation</data>
